window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/a433-65329f88fe3a61b3.json"]={sha256:"65329f88fe3a61b397005c05f019e1de085dde6db3ac58b3aef287d59c4d3e49",value:{"id":"a433","title":"積分球輻射量測","titleEn":"Integrating-sphere radiometry","category":"instruments","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從朗伯漫反射壁面如何把任意方向的光通量變成均勻輻射亮度出發，推導球倍增因子 M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))，再逐步建立塗層、開口、擋板、偵測器、標準燈替代法與自吸收修正，最後以不確定度預算與國家實驗室比對完成總光通量量測系統的驗收。","summaryEn":"Starting from how a Lambertian diffuse wall turns flux from any direction into uniform radiance, this course derives the sphere multiplier M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)), then builds up coating, ports, baffles, detector, standard-lamp substitution and self-absorption correction, and closes with an uncertainty budget and a national-laboratory comparison to accept a total-luminous-flux measurement system.","scope":"依公開物理原理與官方資料編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是原廠配方、施工圖、設備操作許可或安全程序。數值均為教學假設，需依實際規格重算。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public physics and official sources. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, operating authorisation or safety procedures. Numbers are teaching assumptions and must be recalculated for real specifications.","subcategory":"optics-spectroscopy-radiometry","subcategoryTitle":"光譜與輻射量測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Spectroscopy and radiometry","learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-spectroscopy-radiometry","learningTags":["optics","optics-spectroscopy-radiometry","detector"],"architectureFamily":"detector","architectureNodes":[["待測燈或總光通量標準燈（球心）","Test lamp or total-flux standard lamp (centre mount)"],["燒結 PTFE 球腔","Sintered-PTFE sphere cavity"],["擋板與開口","Baffle and ports"],["V(λ) 光度計頭／光譜輻射計","V(λ) photometer head / spectroradiometer"],["輔助燈（自吸收修正）","Auxiliary lamp (self-absorption correction)"],["資料處理與 NIST 追溯","Data processing and NIST traceability"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[4,1],[3,5]],"diagram":{"type":"detector","labels":["待測燈或總光通量標準燈（球心）","燒結 PTFE 球腔","擋板與開口","V(λ) 光度計頭／光譜輻射計","輔助燈（自吸收修正）"],"labelsEn":["Test lamp or total-flux standard lamp (centre mount)","Sintered-PTFE sphere cavity","Baffle and ports","V(λ) photometer head / spectroradiometer","Auxiliary lamp (self-absorption correction)"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"LED 總光通量量測練習：直徑 200 mm 的燒結 PTFE 球，ρ = 0.98、有效開口比 f = 0.03，M = 0.98/(1 − 0.98×0.97) = 19.8；球內表面積 A_s = 0.1257 m²。待測白光 LED 輻射通量約 1 W 時壁面輻照度 E = 1×19.8/0.1257 = 157.9 W/m²，輻射亮度 L = 50.3 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹，1 mm² 矽偵測器收到 0.158 mW、光電流約 52 µA。替代法：標準燈 1000 lm 讀 2.000 V，LED 讀 1.500 V，輔助燈在標準燈與 LED 在位時分別讀 1.040 V 與 1.000 V，自吸收修正 α = 1.040；光譜失配修正 F* = 1.015。Φ_DUT = 1000×(1.500/2.000)×1.040×1.015 = 792 lm。不確定度：u_c = 0.76%（k = 1），U = 1.5%（k = 2），即 792 ± 12 lm。若球壁因污染使 ρ 降到 0.97 而標準燈未在同一天重量，M 由 19.8 降到 16.4，所有結果會偏低 17%——這就是每次量測都要重做替代法的原因。所有數值皆為教學假設。","textEn":"LED total-luminous-flux exercise: a 200 mm sintered-PTFE sphere with ρ = 0.98 and effective port fraction f = 0.03 has M = 0.98/(1 − 0.98×0.97) = 19.8 and interior area A_s = 0.1257 m². For a white LED emitting about 1 W of radiant flux the wall irradiance is E = 1×19.8/0.1257 = 157.9 W/m², the radiance L = 50.3 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹, and a 1 mm² silicon detector receives 0.158 mW, about 52 µA of photocurrent. Substitution: the 1000 lm standard lamp reads 2.000 V, the LED reads 1.500 V, the auxiliary lamp reads 1.040 V and 1.000 V with the standard lamp and the LED in place, so the self-absorption correction is α = 1.040; the spectral mismatch factor is F* = 1.015. Φ_DUT = 1000×(1.500/2.000)×1.040×1.015 = 792 lm. Uncertainty: u_c = 0.76% (k = 1), U = 1.5% (k = 2), i.e. 792 ± 12 lm. If contamination lowered ρ to 0.97 and the standard lamp were not remeasured the same day, M would fall from 19.8 to 16.4 and every result would read 17% low, which is why substitution is repeated at every measurement. All values are teaching assumptions.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":12,"enrichmentVersion":12,"stages":[{"id":"a433-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「積分球的輻射交換原理」與「輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere\" and \"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a433-v12-01","title":"積分球的輻射交換原理：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「朗伯漫反射壁面與球倍增因子」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lambertian wall and the sphere multiplier” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"積分球的內壁是高反射率的朗伯漫反射面：任一點被照亮後向所有方向以餘弦分佈再輻射，而球面幾何的特性是球內任意一點發出的光在其他所有壁面上造成相同的輻照度，與方向無關。於是輸入光通量 Φ 經過無窮多次反射後，壁面輻照度成為等比級數的和，比值由壁面反射率 ρ 與開口比 f（所有開口面積佔球面積的比例）決定。偵測器看到的是這個經過空間積分、與光源方向和分佈無關的均勻輻射亮度，這就是「積分」的意義。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「朗伯漫反射壁面與球倍增因子」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The inner wall of an integrating sphere is a highly reflective Lambertian diffuser: any illuminated point re-radiates in all directions with a cosine distribution, and the geometry of a sphere makes light leaving any point produce the same irradiance on every other part of the wall regardless of direction. The input flux Φ therefore builds up through an infinite series of reflections, and the wall irradiance becomes a geometric sum whose ratio depends on wall reflectance ρ and port fraction f (the fraction of sphere area occupied by all openings). The detector sees this spatially integrated radiance, independent of the source's direction and distribution, which is what integrating means. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Lambertian wall and the sphere multiplier”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：球倍增因子 M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The sphere multiplier is M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)).","failure":"常見誤解：「積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「朗伯漫反射壁面與球倍增因子」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Lambertian wall and the sphere multiplier”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-01-k1","title":"積分球的輻射交換原理","titleEn":"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere","text":"積分球的內壁是高反射率的朗伯漫反射面：任一點被照亮後向所有方向以餘弦分佈再輻射，而球面幾何的特性是球內任意一點發出的光在其他所有壁面上造成相同的輻照度，與方向無關。於是輸入光通量 Φ 經過無窮多次反射後，壁面輻照度成為等比級數的和，比值由壁面反射率 ρ 與開口比 f（所有開口面積佔球面積的比例）決定。","textEn":"The inner wall of an integrating sphere is a highly reflective Lambertian diffuser: any illuminated point re-radiates in all directions with a cosine distribution, and the geometry of a sphere makes light leaving any point produce the same irradiance on every other part of the wall regardless of direction. The input flux Φ therefore builds up through an infinite series of reflections, and the wall irradiance becomes a geometric sum whose ratio depends on wall reflectance ρ and port fraction f (the fraction of sphere area occupied by all openings).","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「積分球的輻射交換原理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere\" is correct?","options":["積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。","積分球的內壁是高反射率的朗伯漫反射面：任一點被照亮後向所有方向以餘弦分佈再輻射，而球面幾何的特性是球內任意一點發出的光在其他所有壁面上造成相同的輻照度，與方向無關。","偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.","The inner wall of an integrating sphere is a highly reflective Lambertian diffuser: any illuminated point re-radiates in all directions with a cosine distribution, and the geometry of a sphere makes light leaving any point produce the same irradiance on every other part of the wall regardless of direction.","The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"積分球的內壁是高反射率的朗伯漫反射面：任一點被照亮後向所有方向以餘弦分佈再輻射，而球面幾何的特性是球內任意一點發出的光在其他所有壁面上造成相同的輻照度，與方向無關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The inner wall of an integrating sphere is a highly reflective Lambertian diffuser: any illuminated point re-radiates in all directions with a cosine distribution, and the geometry of a sphere makes light leaving any point produce the same irradiance on every other part of the wall regardless of direction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"a433-v12-02","title":"積分球的輻射交換原理：定量估算","titleEn":"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「朗伯漫反射壁面與球倍增因子」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lambertian wall and the sphere multiplier” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：球倍增因子 M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))。取 ρ = 0.98、f = 0.03：M = 0.98/(1 − 0.98×0.97) = 0.98/0.0494 = 19.8；ρ = 0.95 時 M = 0.95/(1 − 0.9215) = 12.1；ρ 只從 0.98 掉到 0.97，M = 0.97/(1 − 0.9409) = 16.4，下降 17%。壁面反射率 1% 的變化放大成約 17% 的通量變化，這是積分球量測必須用替代法的根本原因。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The sphere multiplier is M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)). With ρ = 0.98 and f = 0.03, M = 0.98/(1 − 0.98×0.97) = 0.98/0.0494 = 19.8; with ρ = 0.95, M = 0.95/(1 − 0.9215) = 12.1; if ρ merely drops from 0.98 to 0.97, M = 0.97/(1 − 0.9409) = 16.4, a 17% fall. A 1% change in wall reflectance becomes roughly a 17% change in throughput, the root reason sphere measurements must use substitution. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用穩定的 LED 或雷射把已知光通量（先以功率計量得）打入球內，記錄偵測器訊號，再把同一光源的入射方向從正對壁面改成斜射 30°、45°，確認訊號變化小於 0.5%，證明方向無關性；最後以輸入功率、偵測器面積與響應度反推 M，與 ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) 的估計值比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inject a known flux (first measured with a power meter) from a stable LED or laser into the sphere, record the detector signal, then change the entry direction from normal to 30° and 45° off the wall and confirm that the signal changes by less than 0.5%, demonstrating direction independence; finally back out M from input power, detector area and responsivity and compare with the ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) estimate.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"球倍增因子 M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))。取 ρ = 0.98、f = 0.03：M = 0.98/(1 − 0.98×0.97) = 0.98/0.0494 = 19.8；ρ = 0.95 時 M = 0.95/(1 − 0.9215) = 12.1；ρ 只從 0.98 掉到 0.97，M = 0.97/(1 − 0.9409) = 16.4，下降 17%。壁面反射率 1% 的變化放大成約 17% 的通量變化，這是積分球量測必須用替代法的根本原因。","textEn":"The sphere multiplier is M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)). With ρ = 0.98 and f = 0.03, M = 0.98/(1 − 0.98×0.97) = 0.98/0.0494 = 19.8; with ρ = 0.95, M = 0.95/(1 − 0.9215) = 12.1; if ρ merely drops from 0.98 to 0.97, M = 0.97/(1 − 0.9409) = 16.4, a 17% fall. A 1% change in wall reflectance becomes roughly a 17% change in throughput, the root reason sphere measurements must use substitution.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「積分球的輻射交換原理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere\", which statement holds?","options":["只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。","重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。","球倍增因子 M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))。"],"optionsEn":["A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.","Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.","The sphere multiplier is M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))."],"answer":2,"explanation":"球倍增因子 M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f))。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The sphere multiplier is M = ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"a433-v12-03","title":"積分球的輻射交換原理：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「朗伯漫反射壁面與球倍增因子」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Lambertian wall and the sphere multiplier” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用穩定的 LED 或雷射把已知光通量（先以功率計量得）打入球內，記錄偵測器訊號，再把同一光源的入射方向從正對壁面改成斜射 30°、45°，確認訊號變化小於 0.5%，證明方向無關性；最後以輸入功率、偵測器面積與響應度反推 M，與 ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) 的估計值比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inject a known flux (first measured with a power meter) from a stable LED or laser into the sphere, record the detector signal, then change the entry direction from normal to 30° and 45° off the wall and confirm that the signal changes by less than 0.5%, demonstrating direction independence; finally back out M from input power, detector area and responsivity and compare with the ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) estimate. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：把球壁當成普通白漆面、容許 10% 的開口比，倍增因子降到個位數且首次反射光直接進入偵測器，量測值隨光源擺放角度變動 5% 以上，積分球失去積分功能。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the wall as ordinary white paint and allowing a 10% port fraction drops the multiplier to single digits and lets first-bounce light reach the detector directly; readings then vary by more than 5% with source orientation and the sphere no longer integrates.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用穩定的 LED 或雷射把已知光通量（先以功率計量得）打入球內，記錄偵測器訊號，再把同一光源的入射方向從正對壁面改成斜射 30°、45°，確認訊號變化小於 0.5%，證明方向無關性；最後以輸入功率、偵測器面積與響應度反推 M，與 ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) 的估計值比較。","textEn":"Inject a known flux (first measured with a power meter) from a stable LED or laser into the sphere, record the detector signal, then change the entry direction from normal to 30° and 45° off the wall and confirm that the signal changes by less than 0.5%, demonstrating direction independence; finally back out M from input power, detector area and responsivity and compare with the ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) estimate.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「積分球的輻射交換原理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere\"?","options":["用穩定的 LED 或雷射把已知光通量（先以功率計量得）打入球內，記錄偵測器訊號，再把同一光源的入射方向從正對壁面改成斜射 30°、45°，確認訊號變化小於 0.5%，證明方向無關性。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。"],"optionsEn":["Inject a known flux (first measured with a power meter) from a stable LED or laser into the sphere, record the detector signal, then change the entry direction from normal to 30° and 45° off the wall and confirm that the signal changes by less than 0.5%, demonstrating direction independence.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用穩定的 LED 或雷射把已知光通量（先以功率計量得）打入球內，記錄偵測器訊號，再把同一光源的入射方向從正對壁面改成斜射 30°、45°，確認訊號變化小於 0.5%，證明方向無關性；最後以輸入功率、偵測器面積與響應度反推 M，與 ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) 的估計值比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inject a known flux (first measured with a power meter) from a stable LED or laser into the sphere, record the detector signal, then change the entry direction from normal to 30° and 45° off the wall and confirm that the signal changes by less than 0.5%, demonstrating direction independence; finally back out M from input power, detector area and responsivity and compare with the ρ/(1 − ρ(1 − f)) estimate. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"a433-v12-04","title":"積分球的輻射交換原理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「朗伯漫反射壁面與球倍增因子」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Lambertian wall and the sphere multiplier” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"把球壁當成普通白漆面、容許 10% 的開口比，倍增因子降到個位數且首次反射光直接進入偵測器，量測值隨光源擺放角度變動 5% 以上，積分球失去積分功能。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Treating the wall as ordinary white paint and allowing a 10% port fraction drops the multiplier to single digits and lets first-bounce light reach the detector directly; readings then vary by more than 5% with source orientation and the sphere no longer integrates. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：偵測器看到的是這個經過空間積分、與光源方向和分佈無關的均勻輻射亮度，這就是「積分」的意義。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The detector sees this spatially integrated radiance, independent of the source's direction and distribution, which is what integrating means.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把球壁當成普通白漆面、容許 10% 的開口比，倍增因子降到個位數且首次反射光直接進入偵測器，量測值隨光源擺放角度變動 5% 以上，積分球失去積分功能。","textEn":"Treating the wall as ordinary white paint and allowing a 10% port fraction drops the multiplier to single digits and lets first-bounce light reach the detector directly; readings then vary by more than 5% with source orientation and the sphere no longer integrates.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「積分球的輻射交換原理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Radiative exchange inside the integrating sphere\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","把球壁當成普通白漆面、容許 10% 的開口比，倍增因子降到個位數且首次反射光直接進入偵測器，量測值隨光源擺放角度變動 5% 以上，積分球失去積分功能。","偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Treating the wall as ordinary white paint and allowing a 10% port fraction drops the multiplier to single digits and lets first-bounce light reach the detector directly.","The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把球壁當成普通白漆面、容許 10% 的開口比，倍增因子降到個位數且首次反射光直接進入偵測器，量測值隨光源擺放角度變動 5% 以上，積分球失去積分功能。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the wall as ordinary white paint and allowing a 10% port fraction drops the multiplier to single digits and lets first-bounce light reach the detector directly; readings then vary by more than 5% with source orientation and the sphere no longer integrates. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"a433-v12-05","title":"輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「壁面輻照度與偵測器通量」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Wall irradiance and detector flux” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"穩態下壁面輻照度 E = Φ·M/A_s，其中 A_s = 4πR² 是球內表面積；朗伯面的輻射亮度 L = E/π（單位 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹）。與壁面齊平的偵測器開口接收的通量就是 E 乘以它的面積，因此偵測器訊號正比於輸入總通量，比例常數包含 M、A_s、偵測器面積與響應度。量測總光通量時光源放在球心（4π 配置），量測定向光源時光源在開口外照入（2π 配置），量測反射率或穿透率時樣品裝在樣品埠；三種配置的 M 與 f 都不同，校正必須在同一配置下進行。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「壁面輻照度與偵測器通量」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In steady state the wall irradiance is E = Φ·M/A_s with A_s = 4πR² the interior area, and for a Lambertian wall the radiance is L = E/π (in W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹). A detector aperture flush with the wall collects E times its area, so the detector signal is proportional to the total input flux with a constant that contains M, A_s, detector area and responsivity. For total flux the source sits at the sphere centre (4π configuration), a directional source shines in through a port (2π configuration), and reflectance or transmittance samples mount on a sample port; each configuration has its own M and f, so calibration must be done in the same configuration as the measurement. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Wall irradiance and detector flux”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：直徑 200 mm 的球：A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a 200 mm diameter sphere A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「壁面輻照度與偵測器通量」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Wall irradiance and detector flux”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-05-k1","title":"輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流","titleEn":"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent","text":"穩態下壁面輻照度 E = Φ·M/A_s，其中 A_s = 4πR² 是球內表面積；朗伯面的輻射亮度 L = E/π（單位 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹）。與壁面齊平的偵測器開口接收的通量就是 E 乘以它的面積，因此偵測器訊號正比於輸入總通量，比例常數包含 M、A_s、偵測器面積與響應度。","textEn":"In steady state the wall irradiance is E = Φ·M/A_s with A_s = 4πR² the interior area, and for a Lambertian wall the radiance is L = E/π (in W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹). A detector aperture flush with the wall collects E times its area, so the detector signal is proportional to the total input flux with a constant that contains M, A_s, detector area and responsivity.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent\" is correct?","options":["偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。","塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。","穩態下壁面輻照度 E = Φ·M/A_s，其中 A_s = 4πR² 是球內表面積；朗伯面的輻射亮度 L = E/π（單位 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹）。"],"optionsEn":["The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size.","Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness.","In steady state the wall irradiance is E = Φ·M/A_s with A_s = 4πR² the interior area, and for a Lambertian wall the radiance is L = E/π (in W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"穩態下壁面輻照度 E = Φ·M/A_s，其中 A_s = 4πR² 是球內表面積；朗伯面的輻射亮度 L = E/π（單位 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹）。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In steady state the wall irradiance is E = Φ·M/A_s with A_s = 4πR² the interior area, and for a Lambertian wall the radiance is L = E/π (in W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹). The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"a433-v12-06","title":"輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流：定量估算","titleEn":"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「壁面輻照度與偵測器通量」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Wall irradiance and detector flux” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：直徑 200 mm 的球：A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m²。輸入 1 W、M = 19.8 時 E = 19.8/0.1257 = 157.9 W/m²，L = E/π = 50.3 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹。面積 1 mm² 的矽光二極體收到 157.9×10⁻⁶ = 0.158 mW；在 555 nm 取響應度 0.33 A/W，光電流 52 µA。整球對該偵測器的「效率」只有 0.016%，所以積分球是用通量換均勻性的元件。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a 200 mm diameter sphere A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m². With 1 W input and M = 19.8, E = 19.8/0.1257 = 157.9 W/m² and L = E/π = 50.3 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹. A 1 mm² silicon photodiode receives 157.9×10⁻⁶ = 0.158 mW; at a responsivity of 0.33 A/W near 555 nm the photocurrent is 52 µA. The sphere's efficiency onto that detector is only 0.016%, showing that an integrating sphere trades flux for uniformity. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以已校正的功率計量一支 532 nm 雷射的功率，再把它射入球內量光電流，由光電流除以響應度與偵測器面積得到 E，再乘上 A_s/M 回推輸入功率，與功率計值比較；差異應小於塗層反射率不確定度所預測的範圍（約 5–10%）。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the power of a 532 nm laser with a calibrated power meter, then shine it into the sphere and record the photocurrent; divide by responsivity and detector area to obtain E, multiply by A_s/M to recover the input power and compare with the power-meter value; the difference should lie within the range predicted by the coating-reflectance uncertainty (about 5–10%).","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"直徑 200 mm 的球：A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m²。輸入 1 W、M = 19.8 時 E = 19.8/0.1257 = 157.9 W/m²，L = E/π = 50.3 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹。面積 1 mm² 的矽光二極體收到 157.9×10⁻⁶ = 0.158 mW；在 555 nm 取響應度 0.33 A/W，光電流 52 µA。整球對該偵測器的「效率」只有 0.016%，所以積分球是用通量換均勻性的元件。","textEn":"For a 200 mm diameter sphere A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m². With 1 W input and M = 19.8, E = 19.8/0.1257 = 157.9 W/m² and L = E/π = 50.3 W·m⁻²·sr⁻¹. A 1 mm² silicon photodiode receives 157.9×10⁻⁶ = 0.158 mW; at a responsivity of 0.33 A/W near 555 nm the photocurrent is 52 µA. The sphere's efficiency onto that detector is only 0.016%, showing that an integrating sphere trades flux for uniformity.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent\", which statement holds?","options":["直徑 200 mm 的球：A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m²。","待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。","LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。"],"optionsEn":["For a 200 mm diameter sphere A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m².","An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary.","An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up."],"answer":0,"explanation":"直徑 200 mm 的球：A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a 200 mm diameter sphere A_s = 4π×0.1² = 0.1257 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"a433-v12-07","title":"輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流：量測與驗證","titleEn":"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「壁面輻照度與偵測器通量」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Wall irradiance and detector flux” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以已校正的功率計量一支 532 nm 雷射的功率，再把它射入球內量光電流，由光電流除以響應度與偵測器面積得到 E，再乘上 A_s/M 回推輸入功率，與功率計值比較；差異應小於塗層反射率不確定度所預測的範圍（約 5–10%）。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the power of a 532 nm laser with a calibrated power meter, then shine it into the sphere and record the photocurrent; divide by responsivity and detector area to obtain E, multiply by A_s/M to recover the input power and compare with the power-meter value; the difference should lie within the range predicted by the coating-reflectance uncertainty (about 5–10%). Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：把量定向光源用的 2π 配置校正係數直接套用在球心 4π 配置上，開口比與自吸收都不同，總光通量系統性偏差 3–8%，而且不同形狀的燈偏差不一樣。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Applying a calibration factor obtained in the 2π configuration for directional sources to the 4π centre-mount configuration ignores the different port fraction and self-absorption, producing a systematic 3–8% total-flux error that changes with lamp shape.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以已校正的功率計量一支 532 nm 雷射的功率，再把它射入球內量光電流，由光電流除以響應度與偵測器面積得到 E，再乘上 A_s/M 回推輸入功率，與功率計值比較；差異應小於塗層反射率不確定度所預測的範圍（約 5–10%）。","textEn":"Measure the power of a 532 nm laser with a calibrated power meter, then shine it into the sphere and record the photocurrent; divide by responsivity and detector area to obtain E, multiply by A_s/M to recover the input power and compare with the power-meter value; the difference should lie within the range predicted by the coating-reflectance uncertainty (about 5–10%).","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","以已校正的功率計量一支 532 nm 雷射的功率，再把它射入球內量光電流，由光電流除以響應度與偵測器面積得到 E，再乘上 A_s/M 回推輸入功率，與功率計值比較。","積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Measure the power of a 532 nm laser with a calibrated power meter, then shine it into the sphere and record the photocurrent.","An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以已校正的功率計量一支 532 nm 雷射的功率，再把它射入球內量光電流，由光電流除以響應度與偵測器面積得到 E，再乘上 A_s/M 回推輸入功率，與功率計值比較；差異應小於塗層反射率不確定度所預測的範圍（約 5–10%）。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the power of a 532 nm laser with a calibrated power meter, then shine it into the sphere and record the photocurrent; divide by responsivity and detector area to obtain E, multiply by A_s/M to recover the input power and compare with the power-meter value; the difference should lie within the range predicted by the coating-reflectance uncertainty (about 5–10%). Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"a433-v12-08","title":"輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流：失效診斷","titleEn":"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「壁面輻照度與偵測器通量」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Wall irradiance and detector flux” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"把量定向光源用的 2π 配置校正係數直接套用在球心 4π 配置上，開口比與自吸收都不同，總光通量系統性偏差 3–8%，而且不同形狀的燈偏差不一樣。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Applying a calibration factor obtained in the 2π configuration for directional sources to the 4π centre-mount configuration ignores the different port fraction and self-absorption, producing a systematic 3–8% total-flux error that changes with lamp shape. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：量測總光通量時光源放在球心（4π 配置），量測定向光源時光源在開口外照入（2π 配置），量測反射率或穿透率時樣品裝在樣品埠；三種配置的 M 與 f 都不同，校正必須在同一配置下進行。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: For total flux the source sits at the sphere centre (4π configuration), a directional source shines in through a port (2π configuration), and reflectance or transmittance samples mount on a sample port; each configuration has its own M and f, so calibration must be done in the same configuration as the measurement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把量定向光源用的 2π 配置校正係數直接套用在球心 4π 配置上，開口比與自吸收都不同，總光通量系統性偏差 3–8%，而且不同形狀的燈偏差不一樣。","textEn":"Applying a calibration factor obtained in the 2π configuration for directional sources to the 4π centre-mount configuration ignores the different port fraction and self-absorption, producing a systematic 3–8% total-flux error that changes with lamp shape.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「輻射量鏈：通量、輻照度、輻射亮度到光電流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The radiometric chain from flux and irradiance to photocurrent\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。","把量定向光源用的 2π 配置校正係數直接套用在球心 4π 配置上，開口比與自吸收都不同，總光通量系統性偏差 3–8%，而且不同形狀的燈偏差不一樣。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness.","Applying a calibration factor obtained in the 2π configuration for directional sources to the 4π centre-mount configuration ignores the different port fraction and self-absorption, producing a systematic 3–8% total-flux error that changes with lamp shape."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把量定向光源用的 2π 配置校正係數直接套用在球心 4π 配置上，開口比與自吸收都不同，總光通量系統性偏差 3–8%，而且不同形狀的燈偏差不一樣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying a calibration factor obtained in the 2π configuration for directional sources to the 4π centre-mount configuration ignores the different port fraction and self-absorption, producing a systematic 3–8% total-flux error that changes with lamp shape. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"a433-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「塗層材料、開口設計與擋板」與「偵測器、光譜匹配與線性」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Coating materials, port design and baffles\" and \"Detector, spectral matching and linearity\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a433-v12-09","title":"塗層材料、開口設計與擋板：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Coating materials, port design and baffles: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「燒結 PTFE 塗層與開口比」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sintered-PTFE coating and port fraction” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"可見與近紅外積分球多用燒結 PTFE（厚度約 10 mm 才能達到 0.99 的反射率，因為材料半透明）或硫酸鋇漆（約 0.97–0.98，較便宜但易受污染與紫外老化）；中紅外改用鍍金粗化表面，在 0.8–20 µm 保持 0.95–0.98。開口比 f 必須壓到幾個百分點以內，而且入口與偵測器之間要加同材質的擋板，阻止第一次反射光直接進入偵測器；擋板本身也算進有效開口比。樣品埠、燈座與導線都會吸收光，使實際的 f 比純幾何計算大。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「燒結 PTFE 塗層與開口比」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Visible and near-infrared spheres use sintered PTFE (about 10 mm thick to reach 0.99 reflectance because the material is translucent) or barium-sulfate paint (about 0.97–0.98, cheaper but prone to contamination and ultraviolet aging); mid-infrared spheres use roughened gold surfaces holding 0.95–0.98 from 0.8 to 20 µm. The port fraction f must be kept to a few percent, and a baffle of the same material between entrance and detector blocks first-bounce light from reaching the detector; the baffle itself counts toward the effective port fraction. Sample ports, lamp holders and leads absorb light too, making the real f larger than the pure geometric value. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Sintered-PTFE coating and port fraction”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：200 mm 球開 25.4 mm 入口、25.4 mm 樣品埠與 12.7 mm 偵測器埠：開口面積 = 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm²，球面積 125,664 mm²，幾何開口比 f = 0.0091；加上擋板、燈座與樣品架後有效 f 取 0.03（教學假設）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 200 mm sphere with a 25.4 mm entrance, 25.4 mm sample port and 12.7 mm detector port has a port area of 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm² against a sphere area of 125,664 mm², a geometric port fraction f = 0.0091; adding the baffle, lamp holder and sample fixture the effective f is taken as 0.03 (teaching assumption).","failure":"常見誤解：「塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「燒結 PTFE 塗層與開口比」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Sintered-PTFE coating and port fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-09-k1","title":"塗層材料、開口設計與擋板","titleEn":"Coating materials, port design and baffles","text":"可見與近紅外積分球多用燒結 PTFE（厚度約 10 mm 才能達到 0.99 的反射率，因為材料半透明）或硫酸鋇漆（約 0.97–0.98，較便宜但易受污染與紫外老化）；中紅外改用鍍金粗化表面，在 0.8–20 µm 保持 0.95–0.98。開口比 f 必須壓到幾個百分點以內，而且入口與偵測器之間要加同材質的擋板，阻止第一次反射光直接進入偵測器；擋板本身也算進有效開口比。","textEn":"Visible and near-infrared spheres use sintered PTFE (about 10 mm thick to reach 0.99 reflectance because the material is translucent) or barium-sulfate paint (about 0.97–0.98, cheaper but prone to contamination and ultraviolet aging); mid-infrared spheres use roughened gold surfaces holding 0.95–0.98 from 0.8 to 20 µm. The port fraction f must be kept to a few percent, and a baffle of the same material between entrance and detector blocks first-bounce light from reaching the detector; the baffle itself counts toward the effective port fraction.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塗層材料、開口設計與擋板」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Coating materials, port design and baffles\" is correct?","options":["可見與近紅外積分球多用燒結 PTFE（厚度約 10 mm 才能達到 0.99 的反射率，因為材料半透明）或硫酸鋇漆（約 0.97–0.98，較便宜但易受污染與紫外老化）。","塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。","只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。"],"optionsEn":["Visible and near-infrared spheres use sintered PTFE (about 10 mm thick to reach 0.99 reflectance because the material is translucent) or barium-sulfate paint (about 0.97–0.98, cheaper but prone to contamination and ultraviolet aging).","Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness.","A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可見與近紅外積分球多用燒結 PTFE（厚度約 10 mm 才能達到 0.99 的反射率，因為材料半透明）或硫酸鋇漆（約 0.97–0.98，較便宜但易受污染與紫外老化）；中紅外改用鍍金粗化表面，在 0.8–20 µm 保持 0.95–0.98。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Visible and near-infrared spheres use sintered PTFE (about 10 mm thick to reach 0.99 reflectance because the material is translucent) or barium-sulfate paint (about 0.97–0.98, cheaper but prone to contamination and ultraviolet aging); mid-infrared spheres use roughened gold surfaces holding 0.95–0.98 from 0.8 to 20 µm. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"a433-v12-10","title":"塗層材料、開口設計與擋板：定量估算","titleEn":"Coating materials, port design and baffles: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「燒結 PTFE 塗層與開口比」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sintered-PTFE coating and port fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：200 mm 球開 25.4 mm 入口、25.4 mm 樣品埠與 12.7 mm 偵測器埠：開口面積 = 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm²，球面積 125,664 mm²，幾何開口比 f = 0.0091；加上擋板、燈座與樣品架後有效 f 取 0.03（教學假設）。塗層 ρ 從 0.98 提升到 0.99 時 M 由 19.8 升到 0.99/(1 − 0.99×0.97) = 24.9，提高 26%，因此高反射塗層與低開口比同樣重要。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 200 mm sphere with a 25.4 mm entrance, 25.4 mm sample port and 12.7 mm detector port has a port area of 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm² against a sphere area of 125,664 mm², a geometric port fraction f = 0.0091; adding the baffle, lamp holder and sample fixture the effective f is taken as 0.03 (teaching assumption). Raising the coating ρ from 0.98 to 0.99 lifts M from 19.8 to 0.99/(1 − 0.99×0.97) = 24.9, a 26% gain, so high-reflectance coating matters as much as low port fraction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用分光光度計配小型參考球量塗層試片在 250–2500 nm 的半球反射率，確認可見波段 ≥ 0.98 且 250 nm 處不低於 0.95；再以小面積光源掃描球內壁，量偵測器訊號隨入射位置的變化（空間響應分布），確認擋板已消除直接照射的尖峰。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the hemispherical reflectance of a coating coupon from 250 to 2500 nm with a spectrophotometer and a small reference sphere, confirming ≥ 0.98 in the visible and no less than 0.95 at 250 nm; then scan a small source across the interior wall and record the detector signal versus entry position (the spatial response distribution) to confirm that the baffle has removed the direct-illumination spike.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"200 mm 球開 25.4 mm 入口、25.4 mm 樣品埠與 12.7 mm 偵測器埠：開口面積 = 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm²，球面積 125,664 mm²，幾何開口比 f = 0.0091；加上擋板、燈座與樣品架後有效 f 取 0.03（教學假設）。塗層 ρ 從 0.98 提升到 0.99 時 M 由 19.8 升到 0.99/(1 − 0.99×0.97) = 24.9，提高 26%，因此高反射塗層與低開口比同樣重要。","textEn":"A 200 mm sphere with a 25.4 mm entrance, 25.4 mm sample port and 12.7 mm detector port has a port area of 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm² against a sphere area of 125,664 mm², a geometric port fraction f = 0.0091; adding the baffle, lamp holder and sample fixture the effective f is taken as 0.03 (teaching assumption). Raising the coating ρ from 0.98 to 0.99 lifts M from 19.8 to 0.99/(1 − 0.99×0.97) = 24.9, a 26% gain, so high-reflectance coating matters as much as low port fraction.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塗層材料、開口設計與擋板」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Coating materials, port design and baffles\", which statement holds?","options":["重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。","200 mm 球開 25.4 mm 入口、25.4 mm 樣品埠與 12.7 mm 偵測器埠：開口面積 = 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm²，球面積 125,664 mm²，幾何開口比 f = 0.0091。","積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。"],"optionsEn":["Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.","A 200 mm sphere with a 25.4 mm entrance, 25.4 mm sample port and 12.7 mm detector port has a port area of 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm² against a sphere area of 125,664 mm², a geometric port fraction f = 0.0091.","An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"200 mm 球開 25.4 mm 入口、25.4 mm 樣品埠與 12.7 mm 偵測器埠：開口面積 = 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm²，球面積 125,664 mm²，幾何開口比 f = 0.0091；加上擋板、燈座與樣品架後有效 f 取 0.03（教學假設）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 200 mm sphere with a 25.4 mm entrance, 25.4 mm sample port and 12.7 mm detector port has a port area of 2×π×12.7² + π×6.35² = 1140 mm² against a sphere area of 125,664 mm², a geometric port fraction f = 0.0091; adding the baffle, lamp holder and sample fixture the effective f is taken as 0.03 (teaching assumption). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"a433-v12-11","title":"塗層材料、開口設計與擋板：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Coating materials, port design and baffles: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「燒結 PTFE 塗層與開口比」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Sintered-PTFE coating and port fraction” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用分光光度計配小型參考球量塗層試片在 250–2500 nm 的半球反射率，確認可見波段 ≥ 0.98 且 250 nm 處不低於 0.95；再以小面積光源掃描球內壁，量偵測器訊號隨入射位置的變化（空間響應分布），確認擋板已消除直接照射的尖峰。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the hemispherical reflectance of a coating coupon from 250 to 2500 nm with a spectrophotometer and a small reference sphere, confirming ≥ 0.98 in the visible and no less than 0.95 at 250 nm; then scan a small source across the interior wall and record the detector signal versus entry position (the spatial response distribution) to confirm that the baffle has removed the direct-illumination spike. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：硫酸鋇塗層被手指油脂與燈具揮發物污染後在藍光區反射率降到 0.93，藍光 LED 的量測值比紅光 LED 多掉 15%，整套色度量測出現偏黃的系統誤差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Once barium-sulfate coating is contaminated by finger oils and lamp outgassing its blue reflectance falls to 0.93, blue LEDs read 15% lower than red ones, and the whole colorimetric measurement acquires a yellow bias.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用分光光度計配小型參考球量塗層試片在 250–2500 nm 的半球反射率，確認可見波段 ≥ 0.98 且 250 nm 處不低於 0.95；再以小面積光源掃描球內壁，量偵測器訊號隨入射位置的變化（空間響應分布），確認擋板已消除直接照射的尖峰。","textEn":"Measure the hemispherical reflectance of a coating coupon from 250 to 2500 nm with a spectrophotometer and a small reference sphere, confirming ≥ 0.98 in the visible and no less than 0.95 at 250 nm; then scan a small source across the interior wall and record the detector signal versus entry position (the spatial response distribution) to confirm that the baffle has removed the direct-illumination spike.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塗層材料、開口設計與擋板」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Coating materials, port design and baffles\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。","用分光光度計配小型參考球量塗層試片在 250–2500 nm 的半球反射率，確認可見波段 ≥ 0.98 且 250 nm 處不低於 0.95。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.","Measure the hemispherical reflectance of a coating coupon from 250 to 2500 nm with a spectrophotometer and a small reference sphere, confirming ≥ 0.98 in the visible and no less than 0.95 at 250 nm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用分光光度計配小型參考球量塗層試片在 250–2500 nm 的半球反射率，確認可見波段 ≥ 0.98 且 250 nm 處不低於 0.95；再以小面積光源掃描球內壁，量偵測器訊號隨入射位置的變化（空間響應分布），確認擋板已消除直接照射的尖峰。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the hemispherical reflectance of a coating coupon from 250 to 2500 nm with a spectrophotometer and a small reference sphere, confirming ≥ 0.98 in the visible and no less than 0.95 at 250 nm; then scan a small source across the interior wall and record the detector signal versus entry position (the spatial response distribution) to confirm that the baffle has removed the direct-illumination spike. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"a433-v12-12","title":"塗層材料、開口設計與擋板：失效診斷","titleEn":"Coating materials, port design and baffles: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「燒結 PTFE 塗層與開口比」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Sintered-PTFE coating and port fraction” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"硫酸鋇塗層被手指油脂與燈具揮發物污染後在藍光區反射率降到 0.93，藍光 LED 的量測值比紅光 LED 多掉 15%，整套色度量測出現偏黃的系統誤差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Once barium-sulfate coating is contaminated by finger oils and lamp outgassing its blue reflectance falls to 0.93, blue LEDs read 15% lower than red ones, and the whole colorimetric measurement acquires a yellow bias. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：樣品埠、燈座與導線都會吸收光，使實際的 f 比純幾何計算大。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Sample ports, lamp holders and leads absorb light too, making the real f larger than the pure geometric value.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"硫酸鋇塗層被手指油脂與燈具揮發物污染後在藍光區反射率降到 0.93，藍光 LED 的量測值比紅光 LED 多掉 15%，整套色度量測出現偏黃的系統誤差。","textEn":"Once barium-sulfate coating is contaminated by finger oils and lamp outgassing its blue reflectance falls to 0.93, blue LEDs read 15% lower than red ones, and the whole colorimetric measurement acquires a yellow bias.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塗層材料、開口設計與擋板」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Coating materials, port design and baffles\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["硫酸鋇塗層被手指油脂與燈具揮發物污染後在藍光區反射率降到 0.93，藍光 LED 的量測值比紅光 LED 多掉 15%，整套色度量測出現偏黃的系統誤差。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。"],"optionsEn":["Once barium-sulfate coating is contaminated by finger oils and lamp outgassing its blue reflectance falls to 0.93, blue LEDs read 15% lower than red ones, and the whole colorimetric measurement acquires a yellow bias.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp."],"answer":0,"explanation":"硫酸鋇塗層被手指油脂與燈具揮發物污染後在藍光區反射率降到 0.93，藍光 LED 的量測值比紅光 LED 多掉 15%，整套色度量測出現偏黃的系統誤差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Once barium-sulfate coating is contaminated by finger oils and lamp outgassing its blue reflectance falls to 0.93, blue LEDs read 15% lower than red ones, and the whole colorimetric measurement acquires a yellow bias. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"a433-v12-13","title":"偵測器、光譜匹配與線性：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Detector, spectral matching and linearity: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「V(λ) 光度計頭與光譜輻射計」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “V(λ) photometer head and spectroradiometer” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"偵測端有兩條路：光度計頭是矽光二極體加 V(λ) 濾光片組合，直接讀出光度量，但濾光片與 V(λ) 的失配（以 f1' 指標描述，好的光度計約 1.5–3%）在光源光譜與校正燈不同時產生誤差；光譜輻射計透過光纖接到球壁，量出相對光譜後以數值積分得到總光譜輻射通量與光通量，失配問題轉為波長校正與雜散光問題。兩者都要求偵測器在 4 個數量級的通量範圍內線性，並把溫度係數控制在 0.1%/K 以內。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「V(λ) 光度計頭與光譜輻射計」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The detection end has two routes: a photometer head combining a silicon photodiode with a V(λ) filter reads photometric quantities directly, but the mismatch between filter and V(λ) (described by the f1' index, about 1.5–3% for a good head) causes error whenever the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp; a spectroradiometer coupled to the wall by a fibre measures the relative spectrum and numerically integrates it into total spectral radiant flux and luminous flux, converting the mismatch problem into wavelength-calibration and stray-light problems. Both require detector linearity over four decades of flux and a temperature coefficient below 0.1%/K. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “V(λ) photometer head and spectroradiometer”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：光譜失配修正因子 F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ]，其中 s(λ) 是光度計的實際相對響應。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The spectral mismatch correction factor is F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ], where s(λ) is the photometer's actual relative response.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「V(λ) 光度計頭與光譜輻射計」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “V(λ) photometer head and spectroradiometer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-13-k1","title":"偵測器、光譜匹配與線性","titleEn":"Detector, spectral matching and linearity","text":"偵測端有兩條路：光度計頭是矽光二極體加 V(λ) 濾光片組合，直接讀出光度量，但濾光片與 V(λ) 的失配（以 f1' 指標描述，好的光度計約 1.5–3%）在光源光譜與校正燈不同時產生誤差；光譜輻射計透過光纖接到球壁，量出相對光譜後以數值積分得到總光譜輻射通量與光通量，失配問題轉為波長校正與雜散光問題。兩者都要求偵測器在 4 個數量級的通量範圍內線性，並把溫度係數控制在 0.1%/K 以內。","textEn":"The detection end has two routes: a photometer head combining a silicon photodiode with a V(λ) filter reads photometric quantities directly, but the mismatch between filter and V(λ) (described by the f1' index, about 1.5–3% for a good head) causes error whenever the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp; a spectroradiometer coupled to the wall by a fibre measures the relative spectrum and numerically integrates it into total spectral radiant flux and luminous flux, converting the mismatch problem into wavelength-calibration and stray-light problems. Both require detector linearity over four decades of flux and a temperature coefficient below 0.1%/K.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「偵測器、光譜匹配與線性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Detector, spectral matching and linearity\" is correct?","options":["只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。","偵測端有兩條路：光度計頭是矽光二極體加 V(λ) 濾光片組合，直接讀出光度量，但濾光片與 V(λ) 的失配（以 f1' 指標描述，好的光度計約 1.5–3%）在光源光譜與校正燈不同時產生誤差。","待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。"],"optionsEn":["A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.","The detection end has two routes: a photometer head combining a silicon photodiode with a V(λ) filter reads photometric quantities directly, but the mismatch between filter and V(λ) (described by the f1' index, about 1.5–3% for a good head) causes error whenever the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.","An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偵測端有兩條路：光度計頭是矽光二極體加 V(λ) 濾光片組合，直接讀出光度量，但濾光片與 V(λ) 的失配（以 f1' 指標描述，好的光度計約 1.5–3%）在光源光譜與校正燈不同時產生誤差；光譜輻射計透過光纖接到球壁，量出相對光譜後以數值積分得到總光譜輻射通量與光通量，失配問題轉為波長校正與雜散光問題。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The detection end has two routes: a photometer head combining a silicon photodiode with a V(λ) filter reads photometric quantities directly, but the mismatch between filter and V(λ) (described by the f1' index, about 1.5–3% for a good head) causes error whenever the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp; a spectroradiometer coupled to the wall by a fibre measures the relative spectrum and numerically integrates it into total spectral radiant flux and luminous flux, converting the mismatch problem into wavelength-calibration and stray-light problems. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"a433-v12-14","title":"偵測器、光譜匹配與線性：定量估算","titleEn":"Detector, spectral matching and linearity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「V(λ) 光度計頭與光譜輻射計」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “V(λ) photometer head and spectroradiometer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：光譜失配修正因子 F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ]，其中 s(λ) 是光度計的實際相對響應。以 2856 K 鎢絲標準燈校正、量測藍光比例高的白光 LED 時，f1' = 3% 的光度計常算出 F* ≈ 1.015（教學假設）；若不套用修正，光通量系統性偏低 1.5%。光通量本身為 Φ_v = 683 lm/W × ∫Φ_e(λ)V(λ)dλ，所以 1 W 的 555 nm 單色光等於 683 lm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The spectral mismatch correction factor is F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ], where s(λ) is the photometer's actual relative response. Calibrating with a 2856 K tungsten standard lamp and measuring a blue-rich white LED, a photometer with f1' = 3% typically yields F* ≈ 1.015 (teaching assumption); omitting the correction biases luminous flux low by 1.5%. Luminous flux itself is Φ_v = 683 lm/W × ∫Φ_e(λ)V(λ)dλ, so 1 W of monochromatic 555 nm light equals 683 lm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以單色儀或一組窄帶 LED 量光度計頭的相對光譜響應 s(λ)，計算 f1'；同時用同一支白光 LED 在光度計頭與光譜輻射計兩條路徑各量一次光通量，兩者套用修正後應一致在 1% 內。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the photometer head's relative spectral response s(λ) with a monochromator or a set of narrow-band LEDs and compute f1'; measure one white LED's luminous flux through both the photometer and the spectroradiometer path, which after correction should agree within 1%.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"光譜失配修正因子 F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ]，其中 s(λ) 是光度計的實際相對響應。以 2856 K 鎢絲標準燈校正、量測藍光比例高的白光 LED 時，f1' = 3% 的光度計常算出 F* ≈ 1.015（教學假設）；若不套用修正，光通量系統性偏低 1.5%。光通量本身為 Φ_v = 683 lm/W × ∫Φ_e(λ)V(λ)dλ，所以 1 W 的 555 nm 單色光等於 683 lm。","textEn":"The spectral mismatch correction factor is F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ], where s(λ) is the photometer's actual relative response. Calibrating with a 2856 K tungsten standard lamp and measuring a blue-rich white LED, a photometer with f1' = 3% typically yields F* ≈ 1.015 (teaching assumption); omitting the correction biases luminous flux low by 1.5%. Luminous flux itself is Φ_v = 683 lm/W × ∫Φ_e(λ)V(λ)dλ, so 1 W of monochromatic 555 nm light equals 683 lm.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「偵測器、光譜匹配與線性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Detector, spectral matching and linearity\", which statement holds?","options":["LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。","積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。","光譜失配修正因子 F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ]，其中 s(λ) 是光度計的實際相對響應。"],"optionsEn":["An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up.","Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.","The spectral mismatch correction factor is F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ], where s(λ) is the photometer's actual relative response."],"answer":2,"explanation":"光譜失配修正因子 F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ]，其中 s(λ) 是光度計的實際相對響應。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The spectral mismatch correction factor is F* = [∫S_ref·V dλ/∫S_ref·s dλ]·[∫S_DUT·s dλ/∫S_DUT·V dλ], where s(λ) is the photometer's actual relative response. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"a433-v12-15","title":"偵測器、光譜匹配與線性：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Detector, spectral matching and linearity: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「V(λ) 光度計頭與光譜輻射計」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “V(λ) photometer head and spectroradiometer” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以單色儀或一組窄帶 LED 量光度計頭的相對光譜響應 s(λ)，計算 f1'；同時用同一支白光 LED 在光度計頭與光譜輻射計兩條路徑各量一次光通量，兩者套用修正後應一致在 1% 內。線性則以疊加法（兩個光源分別與同時點亮）在 3–4 個數量級內驗證，偏差應小於 0.2%。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the photometer head's relative spectral response s(λ) with a monochromator or a set of narrow-band LEDs and compute f1'; measure one white LED's luminous flux through both the photometer and the spectroradiometer path, which after correction should agree within 1%. Verify linearity by the superposition method (two sources lit separately and together) over three to four decades, with deviations below 0.2%. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：光譜輻射計的雜散光讓深紅與近紅外區出現虛假訊號，與 V(λ) 相乘後雖小，但在藍光 LED 上卻把光通量抬高 2%，而且隨 LED 色溫系統性變化。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Stray light in the spectroradiometer produces false signal in the deep red and near infrared; although small after weighting by V(λ), it raises blue-LED luminous flux by 2% and the error shifts systematically with LED colour temperature.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以單色儀或一組窄帶 LED 量光度計頭的相對光譜響應 s(λ)，計算 f1'；同時用同一支白光 LED 在光度計頭與光譜輻射計兩條路徑各量一次光通量，兩者套用修正後應一致在 1% 內。線性則以疊加法（兩個光源分別與同時點亮）在 3–4 個數量級內驗證，偏差應小於 0.2%。","textEn":"Measure the photometer head's relative spectral response s(λ) with a monochromator or a set of narrow-band LEDs and compute f1'; measure one white LED's luminous flux through both the photometer and the spectroradiometer path, which after correction should agree within 1%. Verify linearity by the superposition method (two sources lit separately and together) over three to four decades, with deviations below 0.2%.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「偵測器、光譜匹配與線性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Detector, spectral matching and linearity\"?","options":["以單色儀或一組窄帶 LED 量光度計頭的相對光譜響應 s(λ)，計算 f1'。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["Measure the photometer head's relative spectral response s(λ) with a monochromator or a set of narrow-band LEDs and compute f1'.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以單色儀或一組窄帶 LED 量光度計頭的相對光譜響應 s(λ)，計算 f1'；同時用同一支白光 LED 在光度計頭與光譜輻射計兩條路徑各量一次光通量，兩者套用修正後應一致在 1% 內。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the photometer head's relative spectral response s(λ) with a monochromator or a set of narrow-band LEDs and compute f1'; measure one white LED's luminous flux through both the photometer and the spectroradiometer path, which after correction should agree within 1%. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"a433-v12-16","title":"偵測器、光譜匹配與線性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Detector, spectral matching and linearity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「V(λ) 光度計頭與光譜輻射計」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “V(λ) photometer head and spectroradiometer” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"光譜輻射計的雜散光讓深紅與近紅外區出現虛假訊號，與 V(λ) 相乘後雖小，但在藍光 LED 上卻把光通量抬高 2%，而且隨 LED 色溫系統性變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Stray light in the spectroradiometer produces false signal in the deep red and near infrared; although small after weighting by V(λ), it raises blue-LED luminous flux by 2% and the error shifts systematically with LED colour temperature. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：兩者都要求偵測器在 4 個數量級的通量範圍內線性，並把溫度係數控制在 0.1%/K 以內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Both require detector linearity over four decades of flux and a temperature coefficient below 0.1%/K.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"光譜輻射計的雜散光讓深紅與近紅外區出現虛假訊號，與 V(λ) 相乘後雖小，但在藍光 LED 上卻把光通量抬高 2%，而且隨 LED 色溫系統性變化。","textEn":"Stray light in the spectroradiometer produces false signal in the deep red and near infrared; although small after weighting by V(λ), it raises blue-LED luminous flux by 2% and the error shifts systematically with LED colour temperature.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「偵測器、光譜匹配與線性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Detector, spectral matching and linearity\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","光譜輻射計的雜散光讓深紅與近紅外區出現虛假訊號，與 V(λ) 相乘後雖小，但在藍光 LED 上卻把光通量抬高 2%，而且隨 LED 色溫系統性變化。","待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Stray light in the spectroradiometer produces false signal in the deep red and near infrared.","An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"光譜輻射計的雜散光讓深紅與近紅外區出現虛假訊號，與 V(λ) 相乘後雖小，但在藍光 LED 上卻把光通量抬高 2%，而且隨 LED 色溫系統性變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Stray light in the spectroradiometer produces false signal in the deep red and near infrared; although small after weighting by V(λ), it raises blue-LED luminous flux by 2% and the error shifts systematically with LED colour temperature. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"a433-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「替代法校正與自吸收修正」與「不確定度來源與合成」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction\" and \"Uncertainty sources and their combination\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a433-v12-17","title":"替代法校正與自吸收修正：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「總光通量標準燈與輔助燈」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Total-flux standard lamp and auxiliary lamp” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"因為 M 對 ρ 極敏感，絕對量測不可行，積分球永遠用替代法：先把可追溯至 NIST 等國家實驗室的總光通量標準燈放在球心讀訊號 S_ref，再換上待測燈讀 S_DUT，比值乘以標準燈的認證值就是待測光通量。但待測燈的燈體、燈座與反射罩會吸收球內的光，改變 M；於是球壁上裝一支輔助燈，分別在標準燈與待測燈在位（均不點亮）時點亮輔助燈讀訊號，兩者比值就是自吸收修正因子。標準燈的電流、預熱時間與極性必須按證書操作，否則認證值失效。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「總光通量標準燈與輔助燈」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Because M is so sensitive to ρ, absolute measurement is impractical and spheres always use substitution: a total-luminous-flux standard lamp traceable to a national laboratory such as NIST is placed at the centre and read as S_ref, then the device under test is read as S_DUT, and the ratio times the certified value gives the test flux. But the test lamp's envelope, holder and reflector absorb light inside the sphere and change M, so an auxiliary lamp mounted on the wall is lit with the standard lamp and then with the test lamp in place (both unlit), and the ratio of those readings is the self-absorption correction factor. The standard lamp's current, warm-up time and polarity must follow its certificate or the certified value no longer applies. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Total-flux standard lamp and auxiliary lamp”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：標準燈 Φ_ref = 1000 lm、S_ref = 2.000 V、待測燈 S_DUT = 1.500 V；輔助燈在標準燈在位時讀 1.040 V、待測燈在位時讀 1.000 V，自吸收修正 α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With a standard lamp Φ_ref = 1000 lm reading S_ref = 2.000 V and a test lamp reading S_DUT = 1.500 V, and the auxiliary lamp reading 1.040 V with the standard lamp in place and 1.000 V with the test lamp in place, the self-absorption correction is α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040. Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm; ignoring self-absorption gives 750 lm, 3.8% low.","failure":"常見誤解：「待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「總光通量標準燈與輔助燈」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Total-flux standard lamp and auxiliary lamp”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-17-k1","title":"替代法校正與自吸收修正","titleEn":"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction","text":"因為 M 對 ρ 極敏感，絕對量測不可行，積分球永遠用替代法：先把可追溯至 NIST 等國家實驗室的總光通量標準燈放在球心讀訊號 S_ref，再換上待測燈讀 S_DUT，比值乘以標準燈的認證值就是待測光通量。但待測燈的燈體、燈座與反射罩會吸收球內的光，改變 M；於是球壁上裝一支輔助燈，分別在標準燈與待測燈在位（均不點亮）時點亮輔助燈讀訊號，兩者比值就是自吸收修正因子。","textEn":"Because M is so sensitive to ρ, absolute measurement is impractical and spheres always use substitution: a total-luminous-flux standard lamp traceable to a national laboratory such as NIST is placed at the centre and read as S_ref, then the device under test is read as S_DUT, and the ratio times the certified value gives the test flux. But the test lamp's envelope, holder and reflector absorb light inside the sphere and change M, so an auxiliary lamp mounted on the wall is lit with the standard lamp and then with the test lamp in place (both unlit), and the ratio of those readings is the self-absorption correction factor.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「替代法校正與自吸收修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction\" is correct?","options":["待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。","重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。","因為 M 對 ρ 極敏感，絕對量測不可行，積分球永遠用替代法：先把可追溯至 NIST 等國家實驗室的總光通量標準燈放在球心讀訊號 S_ref，再換上待測燈讀 S_DUT，比值乘以標準燈的認證值就是待測光通量。"],"optionsEn":["An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary.","Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.","Because M is so sensitive to ρ, absolute measurement is impractical and spheres always use substitution: a total-luminous-flux standard lamp traceable to a national laboratory such as NIST is placed at the centre and read as S_ref, then the device under test is read as S_DUT, and the ratio times the certified value gives the test flux."],"answer":2,"explanation":"因為 M 對 ρ 極敏感，絕對量測不可行，積分球永遠用替代法：先把可追溯至 NIST 等國家實驗室的總光通量標準燈放在球心讀訊號 S_ref，再換上待測燈讀 S_DUT，比值乘以標準燈的認證值就是待測光通量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Because M is so sensitive to ρ, absolute measurement is impractical and spheres always use substitution: a total-luminous-flux standard lamp traceable to a national laboratory such as NIST is placed at the centre and read as S_ref, then the device under test is read as S_DUT, and the ratio times the certified value gives the test flux. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"a433-v12-18","title":"替代法校正與自吸收修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「總光通量標準燈與輔助燈」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Total-flux standard lamp and auxiliary lamp” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：標準燈 Φ_ref = 1000 lm、S_ref = 2.000 V、待測燈 S_DUT = 1.500 V；輔助燈在標準燈在位時讀 1.040 V、待測燈在位時讀 1.000 V，自吸收修正 α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040。Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm；若忽略自吸收只得 750 lm，偏低 3.8%。若再乘第 4 單元的光譜失配修正 1.015，最終值為 792 lm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With a standard lamp Φ_ref = 1000 lm reading S_ref = 2.000 V and a test lamp reading S_DUT = 1.500 V, and the auxiliary lamp reading 1.040 V with the standard lamp in place and 1.000 V with the test lamp in place, the self-absorption correction is α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040. Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm; ignoring self-absorption gives 750 lm, 3.8% low. Applying the unit-4 spectral mismatch factor of 1.015 as well gives a final 792 lm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：用兩支互相獨立校正的標準燈互量：以 A 為標準量 B，結果應落在 B 的證書值 ±（兩者不確定度合成）內；再把一個黑色吸收體放入球內重做自吸收測試，確認輔助燈法能偵測到 2–5% 的吸收變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check two independently calibrated standard lamps by measuring B against A; the result must lie within B's certified value plus the combined uncertainty of both.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"標準燈 Φ_ref = 1000 lm、S_ref = 2.000 V、待測燈 S_DUT = 1.500 V；輔助燈在標準燈在位時讀 1.040 V、待測燈在位時讀 1.000 V，自吸收修正 α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040。Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm；若忽略自吸收只得 750 lm，偏低 3.8%。若再乘第 4 單元的光譜失配修正 1.015，最終值為 792 lm。","textEn":"With a standard lamp Φ_ref = 1000 lm reading S_ref = 2.000 V and a test lamp reading S_DUT = 1.500 V, and the auxiliary lamp reading 1.040 V with the standard lamp in place and 1.000 V with the test lamp in place, the self-absorption correction is α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040. Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm; ignoring self-absorption gives 750 lm, 3.8% low. Applying the unit-4 spectral mismatch factor of 1.015 as well gives a final 792 lm.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「替代法校正與自吸收修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction\", which statement holds?","options":["標準燈 Φ_ref = 1000 lm、S_ref = 2.000 V、待測燈 S_DUT = 1.500 V。","積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。","偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。"],"optionsEn":["With a standard lamp Φ_ref = 1000 lm reading S_ref = 2.000 V and a test lamp reading S_DUT = 1.500 V, and the auxiliary lamp reading 1.040 V with the standard lamp in place and 1.000 V with the test lamp in place, the self-absorption correction is α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040. Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm.","An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts.","The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"標準燈 Φ_ref = 1000 lm、S_ref = 2.000 V、待測燈 S_DUT = 1.500 V；輔助燈在標準燈在位時讀 1.040 V、待測燈在位時讀 1.000 V，自吸收修正 α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With a standard lamp Φ_ref = 1000 lm reading S_ref = 2.000 V and a test lamp reading S_DUT = 1.500 V, and the auxiliary lamp reading 1.040 V with the standard lamp in place and 1.000 V with the test lamp in place, the self-absorption correction is α = 1.040/1.000 = 1.040. Φ_DUT = Φ_ref×(S_DUT/S_ref)×α = 1000×0.750×1.040 = 780 lm; ignoring self-absorption gives 750 lm, 3.8% low. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"a433-v12-19","title":"替代法校正與自吸收修正：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「總光通量標準燈與輔助燈」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Total-flux standard lamp and auxiliary lamp” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"用兩支互相獨立校正的標準燈互量：以 A 為標準量 B，結果應落在 B 的證書值 ±（兩者不確定度合成）內；再把一個黑色吸收體放入球內重做自吸收測試，確認輔助燈法能偵測到 2–5% 的吸收變化。每次量測都記錄標準燈的電流與累積點燈時數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check two independently calibrated standard lamps by measuring B against A; the result must lie within B's certified value plus the combined uncertainty of both. Then insert a black absorber and repeat the self-absorption test to confirm that the auxiliary-lamp method detects a 2–5% absorption change. Log the standard lamp's current and cumulative burning hours at every measurement. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：標準燈以交流電源點亮且電流偏高 1%，燈絲溫度上升使光通量多出約 3.5%，所有以它校正的量測值全部偏高；證書上的直流電流條件被當成建議而非規定。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Running the standard lamp on AC with the current 1% high raises the filament temperature and adds about 3.5% to its flux, biasing every measurement calibrated against it; the DC current condition on the certificate was treated as advice rather than a requirement.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用兩支互相獨立校正的標準燈互量：以 A 為標準量 B，結果應落在 B 的證書值 ±（兩者不確定度合成）內；再把一個黑色吸收體放入球內重做自吸收測試，確認輔助燈法能偵測到 2–5% 的吸收變化。每次量測都記錄標準燈的電流與累積點燈時數。","textEn":"Cross-check two independently calibrated standard lamps by measuring B against A; the result must lie within B's certified value plus the combined uncertainty of both. Then insert a black absorber and repeat the self-absorption test to confirm that the auxiliary-lamp method detects a 2–5% absorption change. Log the standard lamp's current and cumulative burning hours at every measurement.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「替代法校正與自吸收修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","用兩支互相獨立校正的標準燈互量：以 A 為標準量 B，結果應落在 B 的證書值 ±（兩者不確定度合成）內。","塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Cross-check two independently calibrated standard lamps by measuring B against A.","Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用兩支互相獨立校正的標準燈互量：以 A 為標準量 B，結果應落在 B 的證書值 ±（兩者不確定度合成）內；再把一個黑色吸收體放入球內重做自吸收測試，確認輔助燈法能偵測到 2–5% 的吸收變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check two independently calibrated standard lamps by measuring B against A; the result must lie within B's certified value plus the combined uncertainty of both. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"a433-v12-20","title":"替代法校正與自吸收修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「總光通量標準燈與輔助燈」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Total-flux standard lamp and auxiliary lamp” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"標準燈以交流電源點亮且電流偏高 1%，燈絲溫度上升使光通量多出約 3.5%，所有以它校正的量測值全部偏高；證書上的直流電流條件被當成建議而非規定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Running the standard lamp on AC with the current 1% high raises the filament temperature and adds about 3.5% to its flux, biasing every measurement calibrated against it; the DC current condition on the certificate was treated as advice rather than a requirement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：標準燈的電流、預熱時間與極性必須按證書操作，否則認證值失效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The standard lamp's current, warm-up time and polarity must follow its certificate or the certified value no longer applies.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"標準燈以交流電源點亮且電流偏高 1%，燈絲溫度上升使光通量多出約 3.5%，所有以它校正的量測值全部偏高；證書上的直流電流條件被當成建議而非規定。","textEn":"Running the standard lamp on AC with the current 1% high raises the filament temperature and adds about 3.5% to its flux, biasing every measurement calibrated against it; the DC current condition on the certificate was treated as advice rather than a requirement.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「替代法校正與自吸收修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Substitution calibration and self-absorption correction\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。","標準燈以交流電源點亮且電流偏高 1%，燈絲溫度上升使光通量多出約 3.5%，所有以它校正的量測值全部偏高；證書上的直流電流條件被當成建議而非規定。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.","Running the standard lamp on AC with the current 1% high raises the filament temperature and adds about 3.5% to its flux, biasing every measurement calibrated against it."],"answer":2,"explanation":"標準燈以交流電源點亮且電流偏高 1%，燈絲溫度上升使光通量多出約 3.5%，所有以它校正的量測值全部偏高；證書上的直流電流條件被當成建議而非規定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Running the standard lamp on AC with the current 1% high raises the filament temperature and adds about 3.5% to its flux, biasing every measurement calibrated against it; the DC current condition on the certificate was treated as advice rather than a requirement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"a433-v12-21","title":"不確定度來源與合成：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Uncertainty sources and their combination: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「不確定度預算表」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Uncertainty budget table” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"總光通量的不確定度由標準燈認證值、光譜失配、自吸收、空間響應不均勻（燈的配光與標準燈不同時，球壁各區響應差異會引入誤差）、偵測器線性與漂移、以及重複性等項組成；各項以相對標準不確定度表示，彼此獨立時用均方根合成，再乘涵蓋因子 k = 2 得到擴充不確定度。預算表的價值在於指出哪一項主導：對白光 LED 常是標準燈與光譜失配，對指向性強的燈具則是空間不均勻。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「不確定度預算表」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The uncertainty of total luminous flux combines the standard lamp's certified value, spectral mismatch, self-absorption, spatial non-uniformity (when the test source's intensity distribution differs from the standard lamp, response differences across the wall introduce error), detector linearity and drift, and repeatability; each is expressed as a relative standard uncertainty, independent terms are combined root-sum-square, and a coverage factor k = 2 gives the expanded uncertainty. The value of the table is to show which term dominates: for white LEDs usually the standard lamp and spectral mismatch, for highly directional luminaires the spatial non-uniformity. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Uncertainty budget table”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：相對標準不確定度（k = 1，教學假設）：標準燈 0.50%、光譜失配 0.40%、自吸收 0.20%、空間不均勻 0.30%、偵測器線性與漂移 0.15%、重複性 0.10%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Relative standard uncertainties (k = 1, teaching assumptions): standard lamp 0.50%, spectral mismatch 0.40%, self-absorption 0.20%, spatial non-uniformity 0.30%, detector linearity and drift 0.15%, repeatability 0.10%.","failure":"常見誤解：「重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「不確定度預算表」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Uncertainty budget table”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-21-k1","title":"不確定度來源與合成","titleEn":"Uncertainty sources and their combination","text":"總光通量的不確定度由標準燈認證值、光譜失配、自吸收、空間響應不均勻（燈的配光與標準燈不同時，球壁各區響應差異會引入誤差）、偵測器線性與漂移、以及重複性等項組成；各項以相對標準不確定度表示，彼此獨立時用均方根合成，再乘涵蓋因子 k = 2 得到擴充不確定度。預算表的價值在於指出哪一項主導：對白光 LED 常是標準燈與光譜失配，對指向性強的燈具則是空間不均勻。","textEn":"The uncertainty of total luminous flux combines the standard lamp's certified value, spectral mismatch, self-absorption, spatial non-uniformity (when the test source's intensity distribution differs from the standard lamp, response differences across the wall introduce error), detector linearity and drift, and repeatability; each is expressed as a relative standard uncertainty, independent terms are combined root-sum-square, and a coverage factor k = 2 gives the expanded uncertainty. The value of the table is to show which term dominates: for white LEDs usually the standard lamp and spectral mismatch, for highly directional luminaires the spatial non-uniformity.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「不確定度來源與合成」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Uncertainty sources and their combination\" is correct?","options":["總光通量的不確定度由標準燈認證值、光譜失配、自吸收、空間響應不均勻（燈的配光與標準燈不同時，球壁各區響應差異會引入誤差）、偵測器線性與漂移、以及重複性等項組成。","重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。","LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。"],"optionsEn":["The uncertainty of total luminous flux combines the standard lamp's certified value, spectral mismatch, self-absorption, spatial non-uniformity (when the test source's intensity distribution differs from the standard lamp, response differences across the wall introduce error), detector linearity and drift, and repeatability.","Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.","An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總光通量的不確定度由標準燈認證值、光譜失配、自吸收、空間響應不均勻（燈的配光與標準燈不同時，球壁各區響應差異會引入誤差）、偵測器線性與漂移、以及重複性等項組成；各項以相對標準不確定度表示，彼此獨立時用均方根合成，再乘涵蓋因子 k = 2 得到擴充不確定度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The uncertainty of total luminous flux combines the standard lamp's certified value, spectral mismatch, self-absorption, spatial non-uniformity (when the test source's intensity distribution differs from the standard lamp, response differences across the wall introduce error), detector linearity and drift, and repeatability; each is expressed as a relative standard uncertainty, independent terms are combined root-sum-square, and a coverage factor k = 2 gives the expanded uncertainty. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"a433-v12-22","title":"不確定度來源與合成：定量估算","titleEn":"Uncertainty sources and their combination: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「不確定度預算表」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Uncertainty budget table” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：相對標準不確定度（k = 1，教學假設）：標準燈 0.50%、光譜失配 0.40%、自吸收 0.20%、空間不均勻 0.30%、偵測器線性與漂移 0.15%、重複性 0.10%。合成 u_c = √(0.50² + 0.40² + 0.20² + 0.30² + 0.15² + 0.10²) = √0.5725 = 0.76%，擴充不確定度 U(k = 2) = 1.5%。把標準燈改為 0.30% 的更高等級，u_c 只降到 0.65%，因為光譜失配已成為第二大項。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Relative standard uncertainties (k = 1, teaching assumptions): standard lamp 0.50%, spectral mismatch 0.40%, self-absorption 0.20%, spatial non-uniformity 0.30%, detector linearity and drift 0.15%, repeatability 0.10%. Combined u_c = √(0.50² + 0.40² + 0.20² + 0.30² + 0.15² + 0.10²) = √0.5725 = 0.76%, expanded uncertainty U(k = 2) = 1.5%. Upgrading the standard lamp to a 0.30% class lowers u_c only to 0.65%, because spectral mismatch has become the second-largest term. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：逐項驗證預算：以掃描小光源得到的空間響應分布，配合待測燈的配光曲線數值積分出空間不均勻項；以 10 次重裝重量得到重複性；以光度計與光譜輻射計兩路徑的差異驗證光譜失配項；最後把合成值與連續三個月的管制圖標準差比較，兩者應同量級。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify the budget term by term: integrate the spatial response distribution from the small-source scan against the test lamp's intensity distribution to obtain the non-uniformity term; obtain repeatability from 10 reload-and-remeasure cycles; validate the spectral-mismatch term from the difference between the photometer and spectroradiometer paths; finally compare the combined value with the standard deviation of a three-month control chart, which should be of the same order.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"相對標準不確定度（k = 1，教學假設）：標準燈 0.50%、光譜失配 0.40%、自吸收 0.20%、空間不均勻 0.30%、偵測器線性與漂移 0.15%、重複性 0.10%。合成 u_c = √(0.50² + 0.40² + 0.20² + 0.30² + 0.15² + 0.10²) = √0.5725 = 0.76%，擴充不確定度 U(k = 2) = 1.5%。把標準燈改為 0.30% 的更高等級，u_c 只降到 0.65%，因為光譜失配已成為第二大項。","textEn":"Relative standard uncertainties (k = 1, teaching assumptions): standard lamp 0.50%, spectral mismatch 0.40%, self-absorption 0.20%, spatial non-uniformity 0.30%, detector linearity and drift 0.15%, repeatability 0.10%. Combined u_c = √(0.50² + 0.40² + 0.20² + 0.30² + 0.15² + 0.10²) = √0.5725 = 0.76%, expanded uncertainty U(k = 2) = 1.5%. Upgrading the standard lamp to a 0.30% class lowers u_c only to 0.65%, because spectral mismatch has become the second-largest term.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「不確定度來源與合成」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Uncertainty sources and their combination\", which statement holds?","options":["積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。","相對標準不確定度（k = 1，教學假設）：標準燈 0.50%、光譜失配 0.40%、自吸收 0.20%、空間不均勻 0.30%、偵測器線性與漂移 0.15%、重複性 0.10%。","塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.","Relative standard uncertainties (k = 1, teaching assumptions): standard lamp 0.50%, spectral mismatch 0.40%, self-absorption 0.20%, spatial non-uniformity 0.30%, detector linearity and drift 0.15%, repeatability 0.10%.","Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"相對標準不確定度（k = 1，教學假設）：標準燈 0.50%、光譜失配 0.40%、自吸收 0.20%、空間不均勻 0.30%、偵測器線性與漂移 0.15%、重複性 0.10%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Relative standard uncertainties (k = 1, teaching assumptions): standard lamp 0.50%, spectral mismatch 0.40%, self-absorption 0.20%, spatial non-uniformity 0.30%, detector linearity and drift 0.15%, repeatability 0.10%. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"a433-v12-23","title":"不確定度來源與合成：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Uncertainty sources and their combination: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「不確定度預算表」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Uncertainty budget table” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"逐項驗證預算：以掃描小光源得到的空間響應分布，配合待測燈的配光曲線數值積分出空間不均勻項；以 10 次重裝重量得到重複性；以光度計與光譜輻射計兩路徑的差異驗證光譜失配項；最後把合成值與連續三個月的管制圖標準差比較，兩者應同量級。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify the budget term by term: integrate the spatial response distribution from the small-source scan against the test lamp's intensity distribution to obtain the non-uniformity term; obtain repeatability from 10 reload-and-remeasure cycles; validate the spectral-mismatch term from the difference between the photometer and spectroradiometer paths; finally compare the combined value with the standard deviation of a three-month control chart, which should be of the same order. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：預算表把「標準燈不確定度」與「偵測器校正不確定度」兩項重複計入，又漏掉空間不均勻，報出 0.8% 的擴充不確定度，比對時卻與國家實驗室差 2%，En 值超過 1。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: The budget double-counts the standard-lamp and detector-calibration terms while omitting spatial non-uniformity, reports a 0.8% expanded uncertainty, and then differs from the national laboratory by 2% in a comparison, giving an En value above 1.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐項驗證預算：以掃描小光源得到的空間響應分布，配合待測燈的配光曲線數值積分出空間不均勻項；以 10 次重裝重量得到重複性；以光度計與光譜輻射計兩路徑的差異驗證光譜失配項；最後把合成值與連續三個月的管制圖標準差比較，兩者應同量級。","textEn":"Verify the budget term by term: integrate the spatial response distribution from the small-source scan against the test lamp's intensity distribution to obtain the non-uniformity term; obtain repeatability from 10 reload-and-remeasure cycles; validate the spectral-mismatch term from the difference between the photometer and spectroradiometer paths; finally compare the combined value with the standard deviation of a three-month control chart, which should be of the same order.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「不確定度來源與合成」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Uncertainty sources and their combination\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。","逐項驗證預算：以掃描小光源得到的空間響應分布，配合待測燈的配光曲線數值積分出空間不均勻項。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.","Verify the budget term by term: integrate the spatial response distribution from the small-source scan against the test lamp's intensity distribution to obtain the non-uniformity term."],"answer":2,"explanation":"逐項驗證預算：以掃描小光源得到的空間響應分布，配合待測燈的配光曲線數值積分出空間不均勻項；以 10 次重裝重量得到重複性；以光度計與光譜輻射計兩路徑的差異驗證光譜失配項；最後把合成值與連續三個月的管制圖標準差比較，兩者應同量級。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify the budget term by term: integrate the spatial response distribution from the small-source scan against the test lamp's intensity distribution to obtain the non-uniformity term; obtain repeatability from 10 reload-and-remeasure cycles; validate the spectral-mismatch term from the difference between the photometer and spectroradiometer paths; finally compare the combined value with the standard deviation of a three-month control chart, which should be of the same order. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"a433-v12-24","title":"不確定度來源與合成：失效診斷","titleEn":"Uncertainty sources and their combination: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「不確定度預算表」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Uncertainty budget table” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"預算表把「標準燈不確定度」與「偵測器校正不確定度」兩項重複計入，又漏掉空間不均勻，報出 0.8% 的擴充不確定度，比對時卻與國家實驗室差 2%，En 值超過 1。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"The budget double-counts the standard-lamp and detector-calibration terms while omitting spatial non-uniformity, reports a 0.8% expanded uncertainty, and then differs from the national laboratory by 2% in a comparison, giving an En value above 1. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：預算表的價值在於指出哪一項主導：對白光 LED 常是標準燈與光譜失配，對指向性強的燈具則是空間不均勻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The value of the table is to show which term dominates: for white LEDs usually the standard lamp and spectral mismatch, for highly directional luminaires the spatial non-uniformity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"預算表把「標準燈不確定度」與「偵測器校正不確定度」兩項重複計入，又漏掉空間不均勻，報出 0.8% 的擴充不確定度，比對時卻與國家實驗室差 2%，En 值超過 1。","textEn":"The budget double-counts the standard-lamp and detector-calibration terms while omitting spatial non-uniformity, reports a 0.8% expanded uncertainty, and then differs from the national laboratory by 2% in a comparison, giving an En value above 1.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「不確定度來源與合成」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Uncertainty sources and their combination\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["預算表把「標準燈不確定度」與「偵測器校正不確定度」兩項重複計入，又漏掉空間不均勻，報出 0.8% 的擴充不確定度，比對時卻與國家實驗室差 2%，En 值超過 1。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。"],"optionsEn":["The budget double-counts the standard-lamp and detector-calibration terms while omitting spatial non-uniformity, reports a 0.8% expanded uncertainty, and then differs from the national laboratory by 2% in a comparison, giving an En value above 1.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up."],"answer":0,"explanation":"預算表把「標準燈不確定度」與「偵測器校正不確定度」兩項重複計入，又漏掉空間不均勻，報出 0.8% 的擴充不確定度，比對時卻與國家實驗室差 2%，En 值超過 1。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"The budget double-counts the standard-lamp and detector-calibration terms while omitting spatial non-uniformity, reports a 0.8% expanded uncertainty, and then differs from the national laboratory by 2% in a comparison, giving an En value above 1. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"a433-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性」與「追溯、比對與量測系統交接」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity\" and \"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a433-v12-25","title":"系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「球心燈座、擋板與溫度控制」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Centre mount, baffle and temperature control” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"整合時要決定燈的安裝方式（球心 4π 或開口 2π）、擋板的位置與尺寸（遮住燈到偵測器的直視線但不遮太多壁面）、導線與燈座的顏色與尺寸（白色且最小化），並確保偵測器視野只看到被擋板遮蔽後的壁面。LED 光源的光通量隨接面溫度下降，球內空氣溫度又因燈的功耗上升，所以要等熱平衡並記錄溫度，或以溫控座固定 LED 溫度；大型燈具則須注意球的尺寸應遠大於燈具，否則空間不均勻項失控。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「球心燈座、擋板與溫度控制」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Integration decides how the lamp is mounted (4π at the centre or 2π at a port), where and how large the baffle is (blocking the direct line from lamp to detector without hiding too much wall), the colour and size of leads and holders (white and minimal), and ensures that the detector's field of view sees only baffled wall. LED flux falls with junction temperature while the air inside the sphere warms from the lamp's dissipation, so the system must reach thermal equilibrium with temperature logged, or hold the LED on a temperature-controlled mount; for large luminaires the sphere must be much larger than the luminaire or the spatial non-uniformity term runs out of control. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Centre mount, baffle and temperature control”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：白光 LED 的光通量溫度係數約 −0.3%/K（教學假設）；若球內空氣在 10 分鐘量測中升溫 3 K，光通量漂移 −0.9%，已超過第 6 單元預算中的重複性項 9 倍。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A white LED's flux temperature coefficient is about −0.3%/K (teaching assumption); if the air inside the sphere warms by 3 K during a 10 minute measurement, the flux drifts by −0.9%, nine times the repeatability term in the unit-6 budget.","failure":"常見誤解：「LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「球心燈座、擋板與溫度控制」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Centre mount, baffle and temperature control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-25-k1","title":"系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性","titleEn":"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity","text":"整合時要決定燈的安裝方式（球心 4π 或開口 2π）、擋板的位置與尺寸（遮住燈到偵測器的直視線但不遮太多壁面）、導線與燈座的顏色與尺寸（白色且最小化），並確保偵測器視野只看到被擋板遮蔽後的壁面。LED 光源的光通量隨接面溫度下降，球內空氣溫度又因燈的功耗上升，所以要等熱平衡並記錄溫度，或以溫控座固定 LED 溫度；大型燈具則須注意球的尺寸應遠大於燈具，否則空間不均勻項失控。","textEn":"Integration decides how the lamp is mounted (4π at the centre or 2π at a port), where and how large the baffle is (blocking the direct line from lamp to detector without hiding too much wall), the colour and size of leads and holders (white and minimal), and ensures that the detector's field of view sees only baffled wall. LED flux falls with junction temperature while the air inside the sphere warms from the lamp's dissipation, so the system must reach thermal equilibrium with temperature logged, or hold the LED on a temperature-controlled mount; for large luminaires the sphere must be much larger than the luminaire or the spatial non-uniformity term runs out of control.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity\" is correct?","options":["LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。","整合時要決定燈的安裝方式（球心 4π 或開口 2π）、擋板的位置與尺寸（遮住燈到偵測器的直視線但不遮太多壁面）、導線與燈座的顏色與尺寸（白色且最小化），並確保偵測器視野只看到被擋板遮蔽後的壁面。","積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。"],"optionsEn":["An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up.","Integration decides how the lamp is mounted (4π at the centre or 2π at a port), where and how large the baffle is (blocking the direct line from lamp to detector without hiding too much wall), the colour and size of leads and holders (white and minimal), and ensures that the detector's field of view sees only baffled wall.","An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"整合時要決定燈的安裝方式（球心 4π 或開口 2π）、擋板的位置與尺寸（遮住燈到偵測器的直視線但不遮太多壁面）、導線與燈座的顏色與尺寸（白色且最小化），並確保偵測器視野只看到被擋板遮蔽後的壁面。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Integration decides how the lamp is mounted (4π at the centre or 2π at a port), where and how large the baffle is (blocking the direct line from lamp to detector without hiding too much wall), the colour and size of leads and holders (white and minimal), and ensures that the detector's field of view sees only baffled wall. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"a433-v12-26","title":"系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性：定量估算","titleEn":"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「球心燈座、擋板與溫度控制」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Centre mount, baffle and temperature control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：白光 LED 的光通量溫度係數約 −0.3%/K（教學假設）；若球內空氣在 10 分鐘量測中升溫 3 K，光通量漂移 −0.9%，已超過第 6 單元預算中的重複性項 9 倍。以溫控座把接面溫度穩定在 ±0.2 K 內，漂移降到 ±0.06%。鎢絲燈則相反：點燈後需 10–15 分鐘才達熱平衡，前 5 分鐘的讀值可偏差 1% 以上。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A white LED's flux temperature coefficient is about −0.3%/K (teaching assumption); if the air inside the sphere warms by 3 K during a 10 minute measurement, the flux drifts by −0.9%, nine times the repeatability term in the unit-6 budget. Holding the junction temperature within ±0.2 K on a temperature-controlled mount reduces the drift to ±0.06%. Tungsten lamps behave the opposite way: they need 10–15 minutes to reach thermal equilibrium, and readings in the first 5 minutes can be off by more than 1%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：點亮待測 LED 後每 30 秒記錄一次訊號與座溫，畫出穩定曲線，訂出達到 ±0.1% 穩定所需的等待時間；再以小光源掃描法量 4π 配置下的空間響應分布，確認球壁各區的響應差異在 ±2% 內，且擋板陰影區沒有超過 5% 的凹陷。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After switching on the test LED, log signal and mount temperature every 30 s, plot the settling curve and set the waiting time needed for ±0.1% stability; then map the spatial response distribution in the 4π configuration with the small-source scan, confirming that wall-region responses lie within ±2% and that the baffle shadow shows no dip beyond 5%.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"白光 LED 的光通量溫度係數約 −0.3%/K（教學假設）；若球內空氣在 10 分鐘量測中升溫 3 K，光通量漂移 −0.9%，已超過第 6 單元預算中的重複性項 9 倍。以溫控座把接面溫度穩定在 ±0.2 K 內，漂移降到 ±0.06%。鎢絲燈則相反：點燈後需 10–15 分鐘才達熱平衡，前 5 分鐘的讀值可偏差 1% 以上。","textEn":"A white LED's flux temperature coefficient is about −0.3%/K (teaching assumption); if the air inside the sphere warms by 3 K during a 10 minute measurement, the flux drifts by −0.9%, nine times the repeatability term in the unit-6 budget. Holding the junction temperature within ±0.2 K on a temperature-controlled mount reduces the drift to ±0.06%. Tungsten lamps behave the opposite way: they need 10–15 minutes to reach thermal equilibrium, and readings in the first 5 minutes can be off by more than 1%.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity\", which statement holds?","options":["偵測器收到的通量等於輸入通量除以開口數，與球的大小無關。","只要偵測器是校正過的，光源光譜不同也不需要任何修正。","白光 LED 的光通量溫度係數約 −0.3%/K（教學假設）。"],"optionsEn":["The detector receives the input flux divided by the number of ports, independent of sphere size.","A calibrated detector needs no correction even when the source spectrum differs from the calibration lamp.","A white LED's flux temperature coefficient is about −0.3%/K (teaching assumption)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"白光 LED 的光通量溫度係數約 −0.3%/K（教學假設）；若球內空氣在 10 分鐘量測中升溫 3 K，光通量漂移 −0.9%，已超過第 6 單元預算中的重複性項 9 倍。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A white LED's flux temperature coefficient is about −0.3%/K (teaching assumption); if the air inside the sphere warms by 3 K during a 10 minute measurement, the flux drifts by −0.9%, nine times the repeatability term in the unit-6 budget. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"a433-v12-27","title":"系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性：量測與驗證","titleEn":"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「球心燈座、擋板與溫度控制」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Centre mount, baffle and temperature control” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"點亮待測 LED 後每 30 秒記錄一次訊號與座溫，畫出穩定曲線，訂出達到 ±0.1% 穩定所需的等待時間；再以小光源掃描法量 4π 配置下的空間響應分布，確認球壁各區的響應差異在 ±2% 內，且擋板陰影區沒有超過 5% 的凹陷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After switching on the test LED, log signal and mount temperature every 30 s, plot the settling curve and set the waiting time needed for ±0.1% stability; then map the spatial response distribution in the 4π configuration with the small-source scan, confirming that wall-region responses lie within ±2% and that the baffle shadow shows no dip beyond 5%. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：為了方便接線把黑色矽膠線與金屬支架留在球內，自吸收修正雖能補償平均吸收，但支架在偵測器附近造成局部陰影，指向性燈具的量測值隨方向變動 3%。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Leaving black silicone leads and a metal bracket inside the sphere for convenient wiring lets self-absorption correction compensate the average absorption, but the bracket casts a local shadow near the detector and directional luminaires read 3% differently with orientation.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"點亮待測 LED 後每 30 秒記錄一次訊號與座溫，畫出穩定曲線，訂出達到 ±0.1% 穩定所需的等待時間；再以小光源掃描法量 4π 配置下的空間響應分布，確認球壁各區的響應差異在 ±2% 內，且擋板陰影區沒有超過 5% 的凹陷。","textEn":"After switching on the test LED, log signal and mount temperature every 30 s, plot the settling curve and set the waiting time needed for ±0.1% stability; then map the spatial response distribution in the 4π configuration with the small-source scan, confirming that wall-region responses lie within ±2% and that the baffle shadow shows no dip beyond 5%.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity\"?","options":["點亮待測 LED 後每 30 秒記錄一次訊號與座溫，畫出穩定曲線，訂出達到 ±0.1% 穩定所需的等待時間。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。"],"optionsEn":["After switching on the test LED, log signal and mount temperature every 30 s, plot the settling curve and set the waiting time needed for ±0.1% stability.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"點亮待測 LED 後每 30 秒記錄一次訊號與座溫，畫出穩定曲線，訂出達到 ±0.1% 穩定所需的等待時間；再以小光源掃描法量 4π 配置下的空間響應分布，確認球壁各區的響應差異在 ±2% 內，且擋板陰影區沒有超過 5% 的凹陷。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"After switching on the test LED, log signal and mount temperature every 30 s, plot the settling curve and set the waiting time needed for ±0.1% stability; then map the spatial response distribution in the 4π configuration with the small-source scan, confirming that wall-region responses lie within ±2% and that the baffle shadow shows no dip beyond 5%. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"a433-v12-28","title":"系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性：失效診斷","titleEn":"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「球心燈座、擋板與溫度控制」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Centre mount, baffle and temperature control” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"為了方便接線把黑色矽膠線與金屬支架留在球內，自吸收修正雖能補償平均吸收，但支架在偵測器附近造成局部陰影，指向性燈具的量測值隨方向變動 3%。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Leaving black silicone leads and a metal bracket inside the sphere for convenient wiring lets self-absorption correction compensate the average absorption, but the bracket casts a local shadow near the detector and directional luminaires read 3% differently with orientation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：LED 光源的光通量隨接面溫度下降，球內空氣溫度又因燈的功耗上升，所以要等熱平衡並記錄溫度，或以溫控座固定 LED 溫度；大型燈具則須注意球的尺寸應遠大於燈具，否則空間不均勻項失控。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: LED flux falls with junction temperature while the air inside the sphere warms from the lamp's dissipation, so the system must reach thermal equilibrium with temperature logged, or hold the LED on a temperature-controlled mount; for large luminaires the sphere must be much larger than the luminaire or the spatial non-uniformity term runs out of control.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「LED 一通電就可以量，不像鎢絲燈需要預熱。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An LED can be measured the instant it is powered, unlike a tungsten lamp that needs warm-up.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了方便接線把黑色矽膠線與金屬支架留在球內，自吸收修正雖能補償平均吸收，但支架在偵測器附近造成局部陰影，指向性燈具的量測值隨方向變動 3%。","textEn":"Leaving black silicone leads and a metal bracket inside the sphere for convenient wiring lets self-absorption correction compensate the average absorption, but the bracket casts a local shadow near the detector and directional luminaires read 3% differently with orientation.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「系統整合：燈具安裝、熱平衡與空間均勻性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"System integration: mounting, thermal equilibrium and spatial uniformity\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","為了方便接線把黑色矽膠線與金屬支架留在球內，自吸收修正雖能補償平均吸收，但支架在偵測器附近造成局部陰影，指向性燈具的量測值隨方向變動 3%。","積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Leaving black silicone leads and a metal bracket inside the sphere for convenient wiring lets self-absorption correction compensate the average absorption, but the bracket casts a local shadow near the detector and directional luminaires read 3% differently with orientation.","An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"為了方便接線把黑色矽膠線與金屬支架留在球內，自吸收修正雖能補償平均吸收，但支架在偵測器附近造成局部陰影，指向性燈具的量測值隨方向變動 3%。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Leaving black silicone leads and a metal bracket inside the sphere for convenient wiring lets self-absorption correction compensate the average absorption, but the bracket casts a local shadow near the detector and directional luminaires read 3% differently with orientation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"a433-v12-29","title":"追溯、比對與量測系統交接：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「國家實驗室比對與 En 值」如何決定積分球輻射量測的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “National-laboratory comparison and En value” determines the key performance of “Integrating-sphere radiometry”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"量測系統交接的最後一步是證明它與國家計量體系一致：把一支傳遞標準燈送到 NIST、PTB 或 NMIJ 等實驗室校正，再回到本實驗室以替代法量測，用 En 值比較兩者。En = (x_lab − x_ref)/√(U_lab² + U_ref²)，絕對值 ≤ 1 表示在各自宣告的擴充不確定度內一致。交接文件需包含配置圖、標準燈清單與證書、自吸收與光譜失配修正程序、不確定度預算、管制圖與塗層反射率的定期檢查紀錄，因為塗層老化會使替代法以外的任何快速檢查失效。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「國家實驗室比對與 En 值」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The last step of handing over the measurement system is to prove consistency with the national measurement system: a transfer standard lamp is calibrated at NIST, PTB, NMIJ or a similar laboratory, measured again at home by substitution, and the two results compared through the En value. En = (x_lab − x_ref)/√(U_lab² + U_ref²), and |En| ≤ 1 means agreement within the stated expanded uncertainties. The handoff file must include the configuration drawing, the list of standard lamps with certificates, the self-absorption and spectral-mismatch procedures, the uncertainty budget, control charts and the periodic coating-reflectance check, because coating aging invalidates any quick check other than substitution. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “National-laboratory comparison and En value”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：本實驗室量得傳遞燈 x_lab = 1012 lm、U_lab = 15 lm（1.5%，k = 2）；國家實驗室 x_ref = 1000 lm、U_ref = 8 lm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The home laboratory measures the transfer lamp as x_lab = 1012 lm with U_lab = 15 lm (1.5%, k = 2); the national laboratory reports x_ref = 1000 lm with U_ref = 8 lm.","failure":"常見誤解：「積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「國家實驗室比對與 En 值」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “National-laboratory comparison and En value”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-29-k1","title":"追溯、比對與量測系統交接","titleEn":"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff","text":"量測系統交接的最後一步是證明它與國家計量體系一致：把一支傳遞標準燈送到 NIST、PTB 或 NMIJ 等實驗室校正，再回到本實驗室以替代法量測，用 En 值比較兩者。En = (x_lab − x_ref)/√(U_lab² + U_ref²)，絕對值 ≤ 1 表示在各自宣告的擴充不確定度內一致。","textEn":"The last step of handing over the measurement system is to prove consistency with the national measurement system: a transfer standard lamp is calibrated at NIST, PTB, NMIJ or a similar laboratory, measured again at home by substitution, and the two results compared through the En value. En = (x_lab − x_ref)/√(U_lab² + U_ref²), and |En| ≤ 1 means agreement within the stated expanded uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「追溯、比對與量測系統交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff\" is correct?","options":["積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。","積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。","量測系統交接的最後一步是證明它與國家計量體系一致：把一支傳遞標準燈送到 NIST、PTB 或 NMIJ 等實驗室校正，再回到本實驗室以替代法量測，用 En 值比較兩者。"],"optionsEn":["An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts.","Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.","The last step of handing over the measurement system is to prove consistency with the national measurement system: a transfer standard lamp is calibrated at NIST, PTB, NMIJ or a similar laboratory, measured again at home by substitution, and the two results compared through the En value."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測系統交接的最後一步是證明它與國家計量體系一致：把一支傳遞標準燈送到 NIST、PTB 或 NMIJ 等實驗室校正，再回到本實驗室以替代法量測，用 En 值比較兩者。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The last step of handing over the measurement system is to prove consistency with the national measurement system: a transfer standard lamp is calibrated at NIST, PTB, NMIJ or a similar laboratory, measured again at home by substitution, and the two results compared through the En value. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"a433-v12-30","title":"追溯、比對與量測系統交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「國家實驗室比對與 En 值」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “National-laboratory comparison and En value” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：本實驗室量得傳遞燈 x_lab = 1012 lm、U_lab = 15 lm（1.5%，k = 2）；國家實驗室 x_ref = 1000 lm、U_ref = 8 lm。En = 12/√(15² + 8²) = 12/17.0 = 0.71 ≤ 1，比對通過。若本實驗室把不確定度低估為 5 lm，En = 12/√(25 + 64) = 1.27，反而判為不一致，顯示誠實的不確定度評估是比對成敗的關鍵。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The home laboratory measures the transfer lamp as x_lab = 1012 lm with U_lab = 15 lm (1.5%, k = 2); the national laboratory reports x_ref = 1000 lm with U_ref = 8 lm. En = 12/√(15² + 8²) = 12/17.0 = 0.71 ≤ 1, so the comparison passes. Had the home laboratory understated its uncertainty as 5 lm, En = 12/√(25 + 64) = 1.27 and the result would be judged inconsistent, showing that honest uncertainty evaluation decides the outcome. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：每年至少一次執行傳遞標準燈的往返比對並計算 En；每季以兩支內部標準燈互量，差異超過 0.5% 就啟動塗層反射率檢查；每次維修或清潔球壁後，重新量測空間響應分布與自吸收因子並更新交接文件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run a round-trip comparison with a transfer standard lamp at least yearly and compute En; cross-measure two in-house standard lamps every quarter and trigger a coating-reflectance check if they differ by more than 0.5%; after any repair or cleaning of the sphere wall, remeasure the spatial response distribution and self-absorption factor and update the handoff file.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"本實驗室量得傳遞燈 x_lab = 1012 lm、U_lab = 15 lm（1.5%，k = 2）；國家實驗室 x_ref = 1000 lm、U_ref = 8 lm。En = 12/√(15² + 8²) = 12/17.0 = 0.71 ≤ 1，比對通過。若本實驗室把不確定度低估為 5 lm，En = 12/√(25 + 64) = 1.27，反而判為不一致，顯示誠實的不確定度評估是比對成敗的關鍵。","textEn":"The home laboratory measures the transfer lamp as x_lab = 1012 lm with U_lab = 15 lm (1.5%, k = 2); the national laboratory reports x_ref = 1000 lm with U_ref = 8 lm. En = 12/√(15² + 8²) = 12/17.0 = 0.71 ≤ 1, so the comparison passes. Had the home laboratory understated its uncertainty as 5 lm, En = 12/√(25 + 64) = 1.27 and the result would be judged inconsistent, showing that honest uncertainty evaluation decides the outcome.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「追溯、比對與量測系統交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["本實驗室量得傳遞燈 x_lab = 1012 lm、U_lab = 15 lm（1.5%，k = 2）。","塗層越薄越好，因為薄塗層比較不會剝落，反射率和厚度無關。","待測燈不點亮時放在球裡對量測沒有影響，所以不需要自吸收修正。"],"optionsEn":["The home laboratory measures the transfer lamp as x_lab = 1012 lm with U_lab = 15 lm (1.5%, k = 2).","Thinner coating is better because it does not flake, and reflectance has nothing to do with thickness.","An unlit test lamp inside the sphere has no effect on the measurement, so self-absorption correction is unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本實驗室量得傳遞燈 x_lab = 1012 lm、U_lab = 15 lm（1.5%，k = 2）；國家實驗室 x_ref = 1000 lm、U_ref = 8 lm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The home laboratory measures the transfer lamp as x_lab = 1012 lm with U_lab = 15 lm (1.5%, k = 2); the national laboratory reports x_ref = 1000 lm with U_ref = 8 lm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"a433-v12-31","title":"追溯、比對與量測系統交接：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「國家實驗室比對與 En 值」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “National-laboratory comparison and En value” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"每年至少一次執行傳遞標準燈的往返比對並計算 En；每季以兩支內部標準燈互量，差異超過 0.5% 就啟動塗層反射率檢查；每次維修或清潔球壁後，重新量測空間響應分布與自吸收因子並更新交接文件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run a round-trip comparison with a transfer standard lamp at least yearly and compute En; cross-measure two in-house standard lamps every quarter and trigger a coating-reflectance check if they differ by more than 0.5%; after any repair or cleaning of the sphere wall, remeasure the spatial response distribution and self-absorption factor and update the handoff file. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：實驗室用三年前校正的標準燈持續量測，燈絲蒸發使光通量每 100 小時下降約 0.5%，累積後所有產品的標示光通量偏高 2%，直到客戶在另一個實驗室複測才發現。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A laboratory keeps using a standard lamp calibrated three years earlier; filament evaporation lowers its flux by about 0.5% per 100 hours, all products end up labelled 2% high, and the discrepancy surfaces only when a customer remeasures elsewhere.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每年至少一次執行傳遞標準燈的往返比對並計算 En；每季以兩支內部標準燈互量，差異超過 0.5% 就啟動塗層反射率檢查；每次維修或清潔球壁後，重新量測空間響應分布與自吸收因子並更新交接文件。","textEn":"Run a round-trip comparison with a transfer standard lamp at least yearly and compute En; cross-measure two in-house standard lamps every quarter and trigger a coating-reflectance check if they differ by more than 0.5%; after any repair or cleaning of the sphere wall, remeasure the spatial response distribution and self-absorption factor and update the handoff file.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「追溯、比對與量測系統交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","每年至少一次執行傳遞標準燈的往返比對並計算 En。","重複性很好就表示不確定度很小。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Run a round-trip comparison with a transfer standard lamp at least yearly and compute En.","Good repeatability means the uncertainty is small."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每年至少一次執行傳遞標準燈的往返比對並計算 En；每季以兩支內部標準燈互量，差異超過 0.5% 就啟動塗層反射率檢查；每次維修或清潔球壁後，重新量測空間響應分布與自吸收因子並更新交接文件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run a round-trip comparison with a transfer standard lamp at least yearly and compute En; cross-measure two in-house standard lamps every quarter and trigger a coating-reflectance check if they differ by more than 0.5%; after any repair or cleaning of the sphere wall, remeasure the spatial response distribution and self-absorption factor and update the handoff file. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"a433-v12-32","title":"追溯、比對與量測系統交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"prerequisiteIds":["a433-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「國家實驗室比對與 En 值」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “National-laboratory comparison and En value” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"實驗室用三年前校正的標準燈持續量測，燈絲蒸發使光通量每 100 小時下降約 0.5%，累積後所有產品的標示光通量偏高 2%，直到客戶在另一個實驗室複測才發現。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A laboratory keeps using a standard lamp calibrated three years earlier; filament evaporation lowers its flux by about 0.5% per 100 hours, all products end up labelled 2% high, and the discrepancy surfaces only when a customer remeasures elsewhere. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：交接文件需包含配置圖、標準燈清單與證書、自吸收與光譜失配修正程序、不確定度預算、管制圖與塗層反射率的定期檢查紀錄，因為塗層老化會使替代法以外的任何快速檢查失效。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The handoff file must include the configuration drawing, the list of standard lamps with certificates, the self-absorption and spectral-mismatch procedures, the uncertainty budget, control charts and the periodic coating-reflectance check, because coating aging invalidates any quick check other than substitution.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「積分球校正一次之後就永久有效，因為球本身沒有活動部件。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An integrating sphere stays calibrated forever because it has no moving parts.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a433-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"實驗室用三年前校正的標準燈持續量測，燈絲蒸發使光通量每 100 小時下降約 0.5%，累積後所有產品的標示光通量偏高 2%，直到客戶在另一個實驗室複測才發現。","textEn":"A laboratory keeps using a standard lamp calibrated three years earlier; filament evaporation lowers its flux by about 0.5% per 100 hours, all products end up labelled 2% high, and the discrepancy surfaces only when a customer remeasures elsewhere.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]},{"id":"a433-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「追溯、比對與量測系統交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Traceability, comparison and measurement-system handoff\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","積分球只要內壁是白色的就能把光均勻混合，反射率差幾個百分點無關緊要。","實驗室用三年前校正的標準燈持續量測，燈絲蒸發使光通量每 100 小時下降約 0.5%，累積後所有產品的標示光通量偏高 2%，直到客戶在另一個實驗室複測才發現。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","Any white interior mixes light uniformly, so a few percent of wall reflectance makes no difference.","A laboratory keeps using a standard lamp calibrated three years earlier."],"answer":2,"explanation":"實驗室用三年前校正的標準燈持續量測，燈絲蒸發使光通量每 100 小時下降約 0.5%，累積後所有產品的標示光通量偏高 2%，直到客戶在另一個實驗室複測才發現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A laboratory keeps using a standard lamp calibrated three years earlier; filament evaporation lowers its flux by about 0.5% per 100 hours, all products end up labelled 2% high, and the discrepancy surfaces only when a customer remeasures elsewhere. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4}],"sourceIds":["v12o-labsphere-sphere-theory-applications","v12o-labsphere-sphere-radiometry-photometry","v12o-nist-total-spectral-radiant-flux","v12o-gigahertz-optik-sphere-knowledge-base"],"curriculumVersion":12,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":800}};
